\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won weakens on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2004\par 05:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The South Korean won weakened\par on Friday as indications of increased dollar-buying\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par better-than-expected U.S. current account data helped the\par dollar.\par     The won        lost a quarter of a percent to 1,059 per\par dollar after the Bank of Korea said it had carried out\par "smoothing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the won market in the first half of\par December, boosting the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves by\par $3.4 billion.\par     Analysts said the central banks of South Korea, Singapore\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had stepped up dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since\par November to slow an Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rally triggered by concerns\par that a record U.S. current account deficit would hurt the\par dollar.\par  \par     Stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  make Asian exports, a key source of\par growth in the region, less competitive in the United States.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "With domestic demand still fragile (in South Korea),\par expect such smoothing' behaviour to persist if the won renews\par its strong appreciation trend," ABN AMRO Bank said in a report.\par     The won has led the rally in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 start of October and is Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year, having gained almost 13 percent. It hit a seven-year high  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 near 1,037 per dollar on December 6, but has since lost ground.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It has fallen one percent since the end of November.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar has gained 5 percent and the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore dollar strengthened 3.2 percent as the yen has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciated 2.6 percent this year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showing the U.S. current account deficit was narrower  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 than expected in the third quarter, even though at a record  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high, helped ease some concerns about the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Taken collectively, the data suggests that the financing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the current account deficit was not a major problem in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 third quarter, in the context of solid but not spectacular  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 official inflows," said Alan Ruskin, an analyst at 4CAST, in a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 report.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The bad quarters, in contrast, see the dollar under marked  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pressure, and the current account and financial account data  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for the fourth quarter is likely to provide a far less  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 encouraging picture longer-term," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The third-quarter data came a day after U.S. Treasury  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 figures showed net inflows into the United States in October  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were not enough to cover that month's record $55.5 billion  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TAIWAN DOLLAR, BAHT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar and the Thai baht are expected to lead  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 another Asian rally against a weakening dollar because of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strength of their economies and greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tolerance  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength, JP Morgan said in a report.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Improving labour markets in South Korea, Hong Kong and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore and increased foreign equity investment in South  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea, Taiwan and Thailand would support \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , JP Morgan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The baht weakened a quarter of a percent to 39.25 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar, paring gains made on Thursday after a surprise 25 basis  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 point interest rate rise by the Bank of Thailand.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah lost half a percent on renewed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 concerns about a drop in foreign direct investment and higher  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fuel subsidies which have widened the budget deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, Japan's trade minister, Shoichi Nakagawa, said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia needed to tackle corruption and improve law  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 enforcement if it wanted Japanese investment to return.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at   0309 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.60         104.29       -0.30\par  Sing dlr        1.6450         1.6422       -0.17\par  Taiwan dlr      32.357         32.340       -0.05\par  Korean won     1059.00        1056.30       -0.25\par  Baht             39.25          39.16       -0.23\par  Peso             56.25          56.26       +0.01\par  Rupiah         9315.00        9270.00       -0.48\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.60         107.31       +2.59\par  Sing dlr        1.6450         1.6978       +3.21\par  Taiwan dlr      32.357         33.978       +5.01\par  Korean won     1059.00        1192.00      +12.56\par  Baht             39.25          39.59       +0.85\par  Peso             56.25          55.49       -1.35\par  Rupiah         9315.00        8410.00       -9.72\par  Rupee            43.85          45.60       +3.99.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041217e0ch004mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
