\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee poised for gains, but cbank eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2004\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee will start the\par week on a firm note after having breached the psychological\par 45-per-dollar level in thin trade on Friday, with the U.S. unit\par near lows and talk still strong of a Chinese revaluation.\par     Foreign investment and trade inflows will also support the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but traders will watch for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI) had firmly defended the\par 45-per-dollar mark over most of the past three weeks, but did\par not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday, when the financial hub of Bombay was\par closed for a local holiday.\par  \par     As a result, the rupee firmed past the milestone in\par relatively thin trade, supported by export remittances.\par     On Monday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows will be stronger than\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 usual as they would have bunched up over an extended weekend,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 with the U.S. market closed on Thursday. Most local  \par \par \uc2 transactions are routed through New York.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is benefiting from growing global confidence in  \par \par \uc2 the Indian growth story, while the dollar is struggling amid  \par \par \uc2 doubts about the strength of the U.S. economy, which is running  \par \par \uc2 large deficits.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Foreign funds have invested $6.7 billion in Indian assets\par so far in 2004, the highest ever in a single year.\par     Speculation of a revaluation in the Chinese yuan is also\par supporting Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including the rupee, which is\par trading at a premium in the non-deliverable forwards market.\par     The three-month rupee, for instance, was quoted at 44.77/97\par per dollar on Friday evening.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                                   Previous\par close\par    Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)\par 6,035.03\par    Indian rupee (/$ )\par 44.9850/0050\par    7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)\par 7.2040\par    Call money (%)\par 4.70-4.90\par    6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)\par 0.45\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041129e0bt002xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
