\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indian reserves composition a "dynamic situation".  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Beverly Mathews  \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2004\par 17:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Nov 24 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said the composition of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves could change when asked on Wednesday if the bank was considering boosting its holdings of the strengthening euro.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) does not give a breakdown of its reserves - the world's fifth-largest - but analysts said it may already have reduced the proportion of dollar holdings and would likely continue to do so.  \par \par \uc2 India's reserves, which comprise dollars, euros, sterling and yen in undisclosed proportions, have risen by nearly $23 billion so far in 2004 to a record $123.5 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "The question of composition of reserves ... it's a very dynamic situation. You can't take a view on a daily basis," Governor Y.V. Reddy told reporters on the sidelines of a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has long been held as a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high against it on Tuesday, and again on Wednesday, after the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it could review the share of euros it holds among its $113 billion in reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Asian central banks have been among the largest buyers of dollars as the economic tide turned in their countries' favour leading to massive investment and trade inflows.  \par \par \uc2 These banks were partly looking to build up their ammunition following a crisis in 1997 and to protect their trade competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. unit has declined sharply because of doubts about the fundamentals of the U.S. economy, which is running wide fiscal and trade deficits. It has fallen nearly 4.5 percent against the euro so far in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 "SHIFT PROBABLE"  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, absorbing strong trade and investment inflows to temper a rising rupee , which is up 3 percent to 45.05 a dollar from a 2004 closing low of 46.45 in late July.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Reddy's statement suggested the RBI was following closely the fall in the dollar's value and would adjust the makeup of its reserves accordingly.  \par \par \uc2 "What Reddy tried to say today is that the RBI is dynamically reviewing the situation, which suggests the composition of the reserves will depend on the outlook for various \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said S.P. Prabhu, analyst with IDBI Capital Market Services.  \par \par \uc2 "So they would probably shift to more euros, pounds and yen."  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said they believed the bank may already have been reducing its dollar holdings.  \par \par \uc2 "I would say we have a mixed bag of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and while the dollar may be the single largest, the holding will not be overwhelming," said Saumitra Choudhuri, economic adviser to rating agency ICRA Ltd.  \par \par \uc2 "Our studies suggest we have a significant holding of the euro and the sterling. Because we have diversified our basket over the years based on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlooks, the sharp fall in the dollar will not be much of a concern."  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the RBI will likely continue with its policy of not disclosing the composition of its reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "Its not a good idea for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to talk about this as it doesn't want to give the exact \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  position," Choudhuri said. "Otherwise, people will start anticipating and speculating, which makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's life very difficult."  \par \par \uc2 Negative sentiment towards the dollar was reinforced last week after the Group of 20 rich and developing nations gave no indication they would take action to stem the dollar's fall at a high profile meeting in Berlin.  \par \par \uc2 The United States also appeared to accept the downtrend.  \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said last week that the market appetite for U.S. assets would dwindle, and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows could become insufficient to offset the current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041124e0bo00avv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
