\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee rally seen slowed by cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2004\par 04:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee's rally is seen\par slowing on Thursday as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to\par resolutely peg the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back every time it\par appreciates past the 45 per dollar level, dealers said.\par     "We have seen some really strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the RBI\par (Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) in recent weeks and as long as that\par continues we will see only slow gains for the rupee," a chief\par dealer at a private bank said.\par     "While the dollar's slide against the euro could cause the\par rupee to open quite firmer and at a gap to its previous close,\par we still see a broad range of 44.98 to 45.10 for the day."\par     The rupee          ended at a five-month closing peak of\par 45.0550/0650 per dollar on Wednesday, taking its gains over six\par straight sessions to 0.34 percent.\par     It had appreciated to a session peak of 44.9800 at one\par point before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in, limiting the rupee's\par gains.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the current tight liquidity conditions\par prevailing in the money market were also aiding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  maintain its dollar buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  without worrying\par that it may need to sterilise the rupees entering the banking\par system.\par     "As long as the call money market is tight the RBI does not\par need to worry about the impact of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it\par indirectly helps inject much needed rupee liquidity," the\par private bank dealer said.\par     The call money rate           has been hovering around\par 6.0-6.5 percent, instead of the 4.75 percent -- the reverse\par repo rate -- around which it usually trades when liquidity is\par ample.\par     Money with banks has tightened in view of a strong pick-up\par in bank credit, a slew of bond issuances by state and federal\par governments and recent withdrawals towards festival expenses.\par  \par  -------------------------------------------------------------\par                               MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                              Wednesday's close     Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)      6,016.58         5,996.70\par     Indian rupee (/$ )            45.0550/0650     45.0675/0750\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)          7.1689           7.1397\par     Call money (%)                   6.00/6.25        6.00/6.25\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)      1.67             2.04\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041118e0bi002pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
