\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases early as dollar's rise weighs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2004\par 05:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped early\par on Thursday from five-month highs as the dollar bounced from\par record lows against the euro after the U.S. Federal Reserve\par raised rates and indicated there was more tightening in store.\par     Traders were also wary about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par after the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made aggressive dollar\par purchases in the previous session to curb the rupee's gains.\par     At 9:25 a.m. (0355 GMT), the rupee          was quoted at\par 45.2100/2175 per dollar, down from the previous close of\par 45.1650/1750 -- the strongest since June 11, when it had ended\par at 45.1550/1650.\par     "The rupee should trade between 45.15 and 45.25 against the\par dollar on Thursday," said a chief trader at a private sector\par bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The dollar's recovery after the Fed rate increase and the\par better-than-expected data along with expectations that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not let the rupee gain much are weighing."\par     The dollar bounced back about 1 percent on Wednesday from a\par record low of $1.3006 per euro hit in New York after the Fed\par raised interest rates by a quarter percentage point and said it\par expected to continue raising at a "measured" pace.\par     Also helping the dollar was a larger than expected drop in\par the U.S. trade deficit, since worries about the ability of the\par United States to finance the huge shortfall have been a major\par factor behind the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent downturn.\par     Despite the rupee's early weakness, traders said the\par outlook was upbeat due to strong foreign fund inflows, a drop\par in crude oil prices and continued speculation about a\par revaluation of the Chinese yuan. Crude oil is India's biggest\par import item.\par     But they expected gains by the rupee to be slow, especially\par after India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, Yaga Venugopal Reddy, told\par reporters on Wednesday that high domestic call rates were only\par transitional, giving rise to speculation that the Reserve Bank\par could step up dollar purchases in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par  \par     Its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pumps in rupees into local money market,\par boosting liquidity.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par banks to curb excessive swings in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and has\par bid aggressively for dollars in recent sessions.\par     A cash shortage in the money market has seen call money\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade around 6 percent levels, the highest since  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June. It usually straddles the reverse repo rate of 4.75  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent when liquidity in the banking system is adequate.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ------------------------------------------------------------\par                                MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    9:25 a.m.  Wednesday's close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)      to open         5,973.75\par     Indian rupee (/$ )            45.2100/2175    45.1650/1750\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)      