\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee gives up gains on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2004\par 12:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped from\par intra-day highs to end steady around five-month highs on\par Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively to\par curb the unit's gains, dealers said.\par     The rupee          ended at 45.1650/1750 per dollar,\par marginally firmer than the previous close of 45.1700/1775 --\par the strongest since June 11, when it had ended at 45.1550/1650.\par     Traders said the outlook for the rupee was upbeat due to\par strong foreign fund inflows, a drop in crude oil prices, a\par broadly weak dollar and continued speculation about a\par revaluation of the Chinese yuan. Crude oil is India's biggest\par import item.\par     "Aggressive dollar purchases by the state-run banks, which\par usually act on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , drove the rupee down\par from an intra-day high of 45.1050," said a dealer at a foreign\par bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is probably to ease the liquidity crunch\par in the domestic money market and also perhaps to squeeze out\par banks which had gone short of the dollar."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  usually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par banks to curb excessive swings in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. It bid\par aggressively for dollars on Monday, pulling the rupee down from\par 44.87 per dollar -- its highest since May.\par  \par     Traders said Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could\par lead to a slight easing in liquidity in the money market.\par     A cash shortage in the money market has seen call money\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade around 6 percent levels, the highest since  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June. It usually straddles the reverse repo rate of 4.75  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent when liquidity in the banking system is adequate.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tight liquidity conditions have led to a sell-off in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 federal bonds and are likely to put the government's borrowing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 programme for the rest of the financial year to March 2005 at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 risk.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite steady \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent sessions by the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the rupee is up nearly 1 percent so far this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 calendar year, helped mainly by foreign funds investment in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian equities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreigners, betting on Indian economic growth of at least 6  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent, have bought $6 billion worth of local shares so far  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this year, after a record $6.7 billion for the whole of 2003.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par                                MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                Wednesday's close Tuesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)      5,973.75        5,929.60\par     Indian rupee (/$ )            45.1650/1750    45.1700/1775\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)          7.1475*         7.1768\par     Call money (%)           