\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee eases from 5-mth high, but mood upbeat.  \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2004\par 05:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped from\par five-month highs on Tuesday morning, with traders wary about\par increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb sharp gains by the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     Underlying sentiment was positive, helped by robust foreign\par fund inflows, a broadly weak dollar and on increased\par speculation about a revaluation of the Chinese yuan, which\par might lead to a strengthening of other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     At 9:25 a.m. (0355 GMT), the rupee          was quoted at\par 45.1950/2100 per dollar, compared with its previous close of\par 45.1700/1800 -- the strongest since June 11, when it ended at\par 45.1550/1650.\par  \par     "The rupee is likely to trade in a 45.15-45.25 range\par today," said a chief dealer at a private sector bank.\par     "So far there is no \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but one can't rule that\par out if the rupee starts to gain swiftly."\par     Traders said a shift in Tuesday's spot settlement date to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nov. 16, instead of Thursday due to local and U.S. holidays was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 leading to some technical adjustments, causing the rupee to  \par \par \uc2 ease marginally in early deals.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Banks in Bombay are closed on Friday and Monday for local\par holidays.\par     The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid aggressively for dollars on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday to curb sharp gains by the rupee, which touched 44.87  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 per dollar - its highest since May - before giving up most of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the gains to end at a new five-month high.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian rupee is now up nearly 1 percent so far this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 calendar year, rebounding from a 6.3 percent slump between  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April and July, when foreign investment inflows had slowed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after a left-backed government took office in New Delhi and the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve started to raise interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investments from foreign funds have since revived as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investors bet on robust economic growth. Foreign funds have  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bought nearly $6 billion worth of Indian shares so far this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year, after a record $6.7 billion in the whole of 2003.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market through state-run banks to curb sharp swings.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would lead to a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 slight easing in rupee liquidity in the next few days.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A cash crunch in the money market has seen call money  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade around 6 percent levels, the highest since  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June. It usually straddles the reverse repo rate of 4.75  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent when liquidity in the banking system is adequate.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ----------------------------------