\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee seen firm, but eyes c.bank.  \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2004\par 04:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is seen trading\par firm around five-month highs on Tuesday, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in a bid to increase money market liquidity and likely to mop\par up dollar inflows, dealers said.\par     Underlying sentiment will be helped by a weak dollar, which\par hit record lows against the euro, increased speculation about a\par revaluation of the Chinese yuan and a drop in prices of crude\par oil, India's biggest import.\par     India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively bid dollars on Monday to\par curb sharp gains by the rupee which had touched 44.87 per\par dollar -- its highest since May -- before giving up most of the\par gains to end at a new five-month high.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market through state-run banks to curb sharp swings.\par Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would lead to a\par slight easing in rupee liquidity in the next few days.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A cash crunch in the money market has seen call money\par   trade around 6 percent levels, the highest since\par June. It usually straddles the reverse repo rate of 4.75\par percent when liquidity in the banking system is adequate.\par     The rupee          ended Monday at 45.1700/1800 per\par dollar,\par  marginally firmer than Friday's close of 45.2000/2200. It last\par ended firmer than this on June 11, when it closed at\par 45.1550/1650.\par  \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par                                MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                               Monday's close      Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)    5,930.47           5,891.36\par     Indian rupee (/$ )          45.1700/1800       45.2000/2200\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)        7.2578             7.2212\par     Call money (%)                 5.90/6.10          5.75/6.00\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)    2.68\par 2.79\par  \par ------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041109e0b9003mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
