\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee bounces back after cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2004\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Sept 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee reversed its\par oil-price-induced weak spell and strengthened slightly by\par Wednesday afternoon after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par check its early slide boosted sentiment in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     At 2:25 p.m., the rupee          was at 46.0800/0900 per\par dollar, recouping its early loss of as much as 0.22 percent and\par marginally stronger than Tuesday's two-week closing low of\par 46.1025/1100.\par     "The RBI (Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just turned\par sentiment and exporters started selling (dollars) at every\par level, resulting in some long dollar liquidation as well," a\par dealer at a state-run bank said. "The rupee gained to 46.0750\par at one point."\par     The rupee, which fell to an early low of 46.21, posted its\par biggest single session loss in two months of 0.31 percent on\par Tuesday after oil prices scaled a record peak above $50 per\par barrel, fanning worries about the trade deficit and inflation.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                       2:25 p.m.        11:30\par a.m.\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)       5,490.45\par 5,467.35\par     Indian rupee (/$ )             46.0800/0900\par 46.1550/1650\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)           6.257