\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee rises for 3rd day on talk of IPO inflows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2004\par 13:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The rupee extended gains into a\par third straight day on Thursday as dealers said dollar inflows\par from foreign investors towards India's largest initial public\par offering had started picking up.\par     They said the local unit was also helped by expectations\par that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and soak up\par these dollars, allowing the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to gain and possibly\par cushion the impact of rising oil prices.\par  \par     India imports 70 percent of its crude oil requirements and\par oil comprises nearly 30 percent of the import bill.\par     A spike in crude oil and global commodity prices led to a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  surge in inflation to a three-and-a-half-year high of 7.51   \par \par \uc2  percent, prompting the finance minister to say the government   \par \par \uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take steps to curb the increase.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee  ended at 46.2000/2100, off intra-day   \par \par \uc2  highs of 46.1800 hit in afternoon deals, firmer than the   \par \par \uc2  previous close of 46.3100/3175 and up nearly 0.35 percent for   \par \par \uc2  the week.   \par \par \uc2  "There is talk that dollar inflows towards the Tata   \par \par \uc2  Consultancy Services (TCS) IPO are coming in," said a dealer at   \par \par \uc2  a private sector bank. "We are expecting it to gather pace   \par \par \uc2  before Monday."   \par \par \uc2  Monday is the last day to pay for foreign investors in TCS,   \par \par \uc2  India's top software services exporter, which raised 54.2   \par \par \uc2  billion rupees in Asia's second-biggest tech IPO this year and   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     About 60 percent of the issue was reserved for qualified\par institutional bidders.\par     Despite Thursday's gains, the rupee has lost 5.8 percent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since it struck a 51-month high of 43.5450/5500 on April 7, on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lacklustre foreign capital inflows after a left-backed\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government took charge in May and global monetary tightening.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After pumping in an average of more than $1 billion a month\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par into Indian assets in the first four months of 2004, foreign\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par funds were net sellers of nearly $800 million in May and made\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par only relatively small purchases in the next two months.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Premiums on the forward dollar, however, rose as corporates\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hedged dollar loans raised earlier. The six-month forward\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par premium edged up to close at an annualised 2.82 percent, up\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                         MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                               Thursday's close  Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts) 5,139.77              5,175.16\par     Indian rupee (/$ )           46.2000/2100      46.3100/3175\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)      6.6588               6.5427\par     Call money (%)                  4.50/4.75         4.50/4.75\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%) 2.82               2.80\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA