\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises on talk of TCS IPO inflows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2004\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The rupee inched up on Thursday\par afternoon on talk that dollar inflows towards India's biggest\par initial public offering were starting to trickle in, dealers\par said.\par     The rupee was also helped by expectations that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and soak up these\par dollars, allowing the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to gain and possibly\par cushioning the impact of rising oil prices.\par     India imports 70 percent of its crude oil requirements and\par oil comprises 30 percent of its import bill. Rising oil and\par global commodity prices have pushed inflation to a\par three-and-a-half-year high of 7.51 percent, prompting the\par finance minister to say the government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par take steps to curb it.\par     At 2:15 p.m., the rupee          was quoted at 46.2575/2675\par per dollar, off the morning's 46.3100/3250 and the previous\par close of 46.3100/3175.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There is talk that the dollar inflows towards the Tata\par Consultancy Services (TCS) IPO are coming in," said a dealer at\par a private sector bank. "We are expecting it to gather pace\par before Monday."\par     Monday is the last day to pay for foreign investors in TCS,\par India's top software services exporter, which raised 54.2\par billion rupees in Asia's second-biggest tech IPO this year and\par India's largest IPO ever.\par  \par ---------------------------------------