\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases as high oil prices weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2004\par 06:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on\par Tuesday morning, subdued by crude oil prices scaling new peaks\par and expectations that a possible U.S. interest rate hike could\par lead to a further slowdown in foreign capital inflows.\par     At 9:15 a.m. (0345 GMT), the rupee          was quoted at\par 46.4300/4500 per dollar, weaker than the previous close of\par 46.4100/4300.\par     It has lost nearly 6.2 percent since it struck a 51-month\par high of 43.5450/5500 on April 7 as capital inflows slowed after\par a left-backed federal government took charge in May and a\par global monetary tightening cycle started to bite.\par     "There is good commercial dollar demand lined up which will\par keep the rupee under pressure," said a chief dealer at a\par private bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  "We are expecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in\par soon and prevent the rupee from dipping past 46.45."\par     Steady \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent sessions has\par seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fall by more than 1\par billion dollars for a second successive week on July 30.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves in Asia's fourth-largest economy\par are now down about $2.8 billion from a record $121.11 billion\par on July 16, as foreign capital inflows have slowed on concerns\par about the pace of economic reforms and growth.\par     After pumping in an average of more than $1 billion a month\par into Indian shares in the first four months of 2004, foreign\par funds were net sellers of nearly $740 million in May and made\par only relatively small purchases in the next two months.\par     Analysts said the surge in prices for crude oil, India's\par biggest import item, was also putting pressure on the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     India imports about 70 percent of its crude oil\par requirements and oil is the biggest single item on the import\par bill. It accounted for 30 percent of the country's imports of\par $22.4 billion in the April-June quarter.\par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                         MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                      9:15 a.m.  Monday's close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)       to open        5,233.21\par     Indian rupee (/$ )            46.4300/4500    46.4100/4300\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)          6.5090          6.4684\par    Call money (%)                   4.25/4.50       4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)   to open            2.49\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040810e08a004ek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
