\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves fall on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2004\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Aug 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by more than 1 billion dollars for a second successive week on July 30, mainly due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support a shaky rupee, data showed on Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said a weaker euro, pound sterling and yen, all of which are part of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets that are expressed in U.S. dollar terms, also contributed to the decline.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves dropped $1.26 billion to $118.32 billion on July 30 from $119.58 billion a week earlier, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves in Asia's fourth-largest economy are now down about $2.8 billion from a record $121.11 billion on July 16, but are still up more than $15 billion so far in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 "There could have been some revaluation losses but the main reason for the decline appears to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Indranil Pan, economist at Kotak Mahindra Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets fell by $1.25 billion in the week, while the Reserve Tranche Position with the International Monetary Fund eased by $8 million. Reserves also include gold, special drawing rights in the IMF.  \par \par \uc2 At Friday's close of 46.36/37 a dollar, the rupee has lost about 1.7 percent this year after posting a record 5.2 percent gain in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee, which is only partially convertible, has been under pressure since hitting a 51-month high of 43.545/550 in early April as foreign capital inflows slowed on uncertainty over economic reforms after a shock win for a communist-backed coalition in national elections.  \par \par \uc2 After pumping in an average of more than $1 billion a month into Indian shares in the first 4 months of 2004, foreign funds were net sellers of nearly $740 million in May and made only relatively small purchases in the next two months.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the rupee was also under pressure due to a surge in oil prices, which hit record highs this week.  \par \par \uc2 India imports about 70 percent of its crude oil requirements and oil is the biggest single item on the import bill. It accounted for 30 percent of the country's imports of $22.4 billion in the April-June quarter.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040807e087004v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
