\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases as foreign funds pare exposure.  \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2004\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, July 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped early\par on Thursday, with sentiment subdued by the greenback's overseas\par rise and on dollar purchases by foreign funds who have been\par paring positions in local assets on doubts about growth,\par dealers said.\par     At 10:00 a.m. (0430 GMT), the rupee          was quoted at\par 46.1800/2000 per dollar, weaker than the previous close of\par 46.1250/1350. The rupee, which analysts say is fairly valued on\par a trade-weighted basis, has lost 0.5 percent in the week so\par far.\par     "There is some dollar demand from banks which offer\par custodial services to foreign funds," said a chief dealer at a\par private-sector bank. "But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also seems to be\par there and it looks like it will defend the rupee from falling\par much."\par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run banks to\par curb excessive volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     Traders said the rupee would ease on the back of a widening\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade deficit, which rose to nearly $6 billion in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 April-June quarter from $4.27 billion a year ago, and as  \par \par \uc2 foreign fund inflows waned on fears that insufficient rains  \par \par \uc2 would hurt growth.  \par \par \uc2 The monsoon is vital to the economy, as about 600 million  \par \par \uc2 of the country's more than 1 billion people depend on a farm  \par \par \uc2 sector that accounts for about 22 percent of gross domestic  \par \par \uc2 product.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Foreign funds pumped in $4 billion between January and\par April on hopes of more reforms and robust growth, but have sold\par some $800 million worth of Indian assets in the past 2-=\par months.\par     Traders said the rupee would also remain under pressure as\par the dollar made headway against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's bullish\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic outlook before Congress on Wednesday helped to push  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the dollar to a three-week peak against the euro and a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-month high against the yen in overseas trade.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                   10:00 a.m.   Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)    to open            4,993.76\par     Indian rupee (/$)             46.1800/2000     46.1250/1350\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)       5.8559              5.8368\par     Call money (%)                   4.25/4.50        4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)  to open              1.94\par ----------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040722e07m000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
