\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee extends fall, monsoon concerns weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2004\par 06:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, July 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended its\par fall on Friday morning, weighed down by doubts about the\par economy's prospects following an erratic monsoon and concerns\par over communist objections to the government's reform proposals.\par  \par     The dollar's firm trend overseas added to the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's woes.\par     The rupee          was quoted at 46.1700/1900 per dollar,\par weaker than Thursday's three-week closing low of 46.1100/1200.\par     "Speculators are continuing to buy dollars as the concerns\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over the monsoons and the reforms remain," said a trader at a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 state-run bank. "Unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the  \par \par \uc2 weakening trend might not be reversed."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monsoons are expected to be 3 percent below normal\par this year, with the shortfall seen more intense in the north.\par     Rain is the only irrigation source for two-thirds of the\par country's cultivated land, and shortfalls will hit the key farm\par sector's output and may slow India's economic growth.\par     Traders said they were also worried about growing\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 opposition to the new government's budget proposal to raise the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 limit on foreign direct investment in the rapidly growing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 telecom and insurance sectors.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                      9:20 a.m.   Thursday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)       to open\par 4,888.19\par     Indian rupee (/$)             46.1700/1900\par 46.1100/1200\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)          5.9664\par 5.9472\par     Call money (%)                   4.25/4.50\par 4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)   to open\par 1.82\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040716e07g000hs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
