\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee off highs as cbank appears, fwds lower.  \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2004\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, July 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee came off an\par early peak by mid-morning on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par signalled through state-run banks it was prepared to step in\par and buy dollars to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from gaining too\par sharply.\par     At 11:15 a.m., the rupee          was at 45.7800/8000 per\par dollar, off a 45.49 peak but still firmer than its previous\par close of 45.8800/8900.\par     "Some state-run banks that normally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the RBI\par (Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) have appeared and shown that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not happy seeing too sharp an appreciation and\par that has checked the (dollar) selling spree," a foreign bank\par dealer said.\par     "It looks like they will ensure the rupee does not gain\par beyond 45.65 and so we should see a 45.65 to 45.85 range\par today."\par     Banks had earlier unwound long dollar positions as the euro\par kept the greenback under pressure overseas after unexpectedly\par weak U.S. data last week strengthened a view the U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to continue a measured approach to rate hikes.\par     The rupee's gains follow a prolonged weak spell that has\par seen the Indian unit slip in 10 of the last 12 weeks amid\par worries about dwindling foreign capital inflows.\par     Traders said the lack of strong dollar inflows was ensuring\par that importers continued to bid the dollar. Inflows are\par expected to remain thin until India's new federal government\par bares its tax and investment-related proposals in its maiden\par budget on July 8.\par     Rupee premiums on forward dollars eased slightly after some\par banks transacted buy-sell swaps to gain from an arbitrage\par opportunity existing in the offshore forwards market .\par     The annualised premium on the benchmark six-month dollar\par was at 1.59 percent, just a little lower than Friday's 1.63\par percent.\par  \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    11:15 a.m.          9:30\par a.m.\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)     4,862.62         4,870.58*\par     Indian rupee (/$)            45.7800/8000      45.6700/7000\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)         5.7134            5.7159\par     Call money (%)                  4.25/4.50         4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)     1.59             1.63*\par     * - previous close\par ------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040705e075000nm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
