\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's reserves fall on cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2004\par 13:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, July 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by half a billion dollars in the week to June 25, easing from a record high struck a week earlier, data showed on Saturday, and analysts said the fall was due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Data released on Saturday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in Asia's third-largest economy fell to $119.41 billion on June 25 from $119.9 billion a week earlier.   \par \par \uc2 "It (the fall) is clearly not just the effect of revaluation and shows the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) sold dollars during that week," said Siddharth Mathur, strategist at JP Morgan Securities in Bombay.   \par \par \uc2 "Revaluation and foreign fund sales do not account for the whole amount. There seems to have been an outflow of around half a billion dollars in addition to these two factors," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The decline was almost entirely in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets portion of the reserves, which fell by $530 million. Reserves also include gold, special drawing rights and India's Reserve Tranche Position in the International Monetary Fund.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI said the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets expressed in U.S. dollar terms included the effect of appreciation/depreciation of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held in its reserves such as the euro, pound sterling and yen.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the latest week's fall, India's reserves were up some $17 billion since January, making it the sixth-largest pile in Asia.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the week ended June 25 to stem volatility in the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee slid to an 11-month intra-day low of 46.34 a dollar during that week from the previous week's close of 45.6650/6800. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales helped the rupee trim its losses to end that week at 45.83/85.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI has said it does not target any exchange rate for the rupee, which is only partly convertible, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to moderate volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has come under presure in the past two months as foreign investment inflows slowed down on uncertainty over the pace of economic reforms after national elections brought a Communist-backed government to power.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have sold more than $900 million worth of Indian bonds and shares since May on those fears.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has in turn suffered. It ended Friday at 45.88/89 a dollar, some 5 percent down from a 51-month peak of 43.545/550 struck in early April.   \par \par \uc2 It is down about 0.6 percent against the dollar in 2004, following a record 5.24 percent gain last year.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040703e073005h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
