\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Falls To 46.00/Dlr; Lowest Since Sep 8, 2003  \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2004\par 08:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee resumed its fall against the dollar Monday, briefly testing the key INR46 support as a panic sell-off in local equities fueled fears of heavy capital outflows.  \par \par \uc2 However, the local unit quickly pared its losses on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-selling by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0655 GMT, the dollar was at 45.92 rupees, off an earlier eight-month high of INR46.00. It had closed at INR45.60 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "Foreign investors seem to be very bearish on the local markets for now on fears that the new government may be less market-friendly than the previous one, and may possibly backtrack on some of the key economic reforms like privatization," said a dealer with a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 An attractive arbitrage opportunity between the local market and offshore markets added fuel to the dollar-buying in the Indian market. Some foreign banks bought the dollar in the local market to sell it at a higher rate offshore, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "It's difficult to take an exact forward view on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in such a volatile market," said a local analyst. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will basically take cues from stocks, to predict likely flows of foreign capital. However, a further sharp fall from current levels may be prevented by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires; 9122-2288-4212; anil.varma@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Shishir Mudgil [ 17-05-04 0716GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040517e05h000df\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
