\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India FX \highlight\uc2  reserves at new peak on cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2004\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, April 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record $117.59 billion in the week ended April 16 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to mop up a bulk of the overseas capital flowing into the country, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , showed India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by $1.53 billion from $116.06 billion in the week ended April 9.  \par \par \uc2 The weekly rise was however less than half the previous week's $3.37 billion increase - which was one of the highest weekly gains.  \par \par \uc2 The pace of the reserve build-up in recent weeks has made Asia's sixth-largest pile of reserves one of the fastest growing as well, having risen 16.9 percent so far in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets expressed in U.S. dollar terms included the effect of appreciation/depreciation of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held in its reserves such as the euro, pound sterling and yen.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts sadid reserve accumulation largely reflects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's determination to stem sharp gains by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, which has rebounded overseas in recent sessions, to protect export competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 "The reserves growth continues to reflect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management measures being undertaken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of strong capital flows into the economy," said Siddharth Mathur, strategist at JP Morgan Chase, Bombay.  \par \par \uc2 "And given that this has happened in the backdrop of the dollar's appreciation versus the euro and other majors means that in real terms the accretion should have been slightly higher."  \par \par \uc2 BUOYANT PORTFOLIO FLOWS  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said overseas funds appeared unperturbed by the country's massive general election which began on April 20 and ends on May 10 and continued to pour money into local assets.  \par \par \uc2 Their net purchases of shares and debt so far in 2004 total $4.4 billion, already more than half the $7.7 billion they invested in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 "With the elections going on, one would have expected foreign capital flows to somewhat ease this month. But that does not appear to be happening," said Saumitra Chaudhuri, economic adviser at Indian credit rating agency, ICRA.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the fact that the Reserve Bank of India had armed itself with new stabilisation bonds to offset the effects of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the new fiscal year from April 1, was likely a key factor in its stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can now tap into securities of up to 600 billion rupees ($13.6 billion) to drain the rupee funds it injects into the banking system every time it buys dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has been grappling with steady foreign capital inflows in the past two years, had almost run out of rupee assets towards the latter half of March, when it briefly loosened its grip on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 That sparked a rupee rally that took the unit to a 51-month closing high of 43.5450/5500 per dollar on April 7, before the Reserve Bank of India reasserted its grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee ended Friday at 44.0350/0450 per dollar, taking its losses over the past two weeks to nearly one percent.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is, however, still 3.5 percent firmer against the dollar in 2004, as foreign capital surges into the Indian economy, which is estimated to have grown by 8.1 percent in the financial year to March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Asia's third-largest economy is forecast to expand by more than six percent in the current fiscal on expectations of a second year of good monsoon rains in the farm-dependent economy.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040424e04o0053d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
