\par\par \b \uc2 Indian shares drop 1 pct on nerves before election.   \b0\par\par\uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2004\par 15:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Anirban Nag\par     BOMBAY, April 19 (Reuters) - Indian shares shed one percent\par on Monday, a day before the general election for the national\par parliament starts, with investors worried about whether or not\par the next government will speed up market-friendly reforms.\par     The rupee ended flat as the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep it down, while federal bonds fell on\par expectations the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may issue more to soak up rupees\par in the money market flowing from its dollar-buying spree in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     The 30-share Bombay Stock Exchange benchmark index\par fell 1.04 percent to 5,800.54 points, retreating from highs\par last week not seen since the government flooded the market with\par around $3 billion worth of shares in state-run companies in\par early March.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There is a certain amount of buyer fatigue after the\par recent listings, and there is also some uncertainty with regard\par to the elections and the monsoon," said Shankar Char, a head of\par institutional sales at Cholamandalam Securities.\par  \par     "So investors are holding on to their normal positions and\par not over-extending them," he said.\par     While quarterly earnings and guidance have been good to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 better-than-expected so far, investors are looking to the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 election and what is forecast to be a "near normal" monsoon for   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cues, he added.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's parliamentary election, which runs from April 20 to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 10, is expected to return the Bharatiya Janata Party-led   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 coalition to power. But doubts remain over its margin of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 victory, which will determine the pace of reforms and economic   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growth.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The run-up to the election has also been marred by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 accidents and sporadic instances of violence. Tuesday's voting   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 will take place in 13 of the 29 states.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The index will remain volatile and range-bound, with a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sustained upward movement possible only beyond the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5,950-level," Char said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Index heavyweight Reliance Industries Ltd (RELI.BO) slipped   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.2 percent to 552.45 rupees, and other industrials fell   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 despite expectations of strong demand in India's bustling   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Grasim Industries Ltd (GRAS.BO), the No. 3 cement producer,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fell 2.5 percent to 1,143.50 rupees. Tata Motors Ltd (TAMO.BO),   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the biggest vehicle maker, dropped 3.5 percent to 487.75   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rupees.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tata Iron and Steel Co (TISC.BO), the second-largest steel   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 maker, shed one percent to 391.45 rupees, while power equipment   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 maker Bharat Heavy Electricals Ltd (BHEL.BO) slid 4.3 percent   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to 612.30 rupees.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee closed at 43.8900/9000 per dollar, off   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 an early intra-day peak of 43.7900, and slightly below Friday's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 43.8850/8950 as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drained the market of dollars.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the 10-year benchmark bond ended   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at 5.0679 percent, up from its previous close of 5.0603   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent. It had slid five basis points last week.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                             MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                  Monday's close    Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)       5,800.54\par 5,861.63\par     Indian rupee (/$)              43.8900/9000\par 43.8850/8950\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)           5.0679\par 5.0603\par     Call money (%)                    4.00/4.25\par 4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium\par        (discount) (%)                    (0.27)\par (0.10)\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040419e04j0020q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
