\par\par \b \uc2 Indian bonds end off peaks on low bond sale cut-off.   \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2004\par 14:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, April 8 (Reuters) - Indian bonds ended Thursday\par just off the day's peaks after a lower-than-expected cut-off\par price at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's sale of market stabilisation bonds\par sparked a little profit-taking, dealers said.\par     The yield on the popular 13-year 8.07 percent bond\par   closed at 5.3475 percent, out of a trough of\par 5.3418 percent but still lower than Wednesday's close of 5.3614\par percent.\par     The 10-year bond's              yield also ended one basis\par point lower at 5.1118 percent, compared to its previous close\par of 5.1219 percent. It had traded as low as 5.1095 percent\par earlier.\par     "The cut-off was a bit of a negative surprise, but then the\par higher weighted average price helped ensure that the fall in\par prices was marginal," a dealer at a mutual fund said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "If inflation comes in low as expected, we should see\par prices moving up again next week, since the rupee inflows from\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are still sizeable."\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a cut-off price of 102.11\par rupees at its sale of the 6.18 percent 2005 bond for 50 billion\par rupees. This was lower than the median forecast of 102.19\par rupees in a Reuters poll of 25 traders.\par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the weighted average of bids it\par received was higher at 102.17 rupees, reflecting market\par appetite.\par  \par     Traders said they would now look fora'\par gweek.\par     Authorities will release data on the wholesale price index\par around noon on Friday, though markets will be closed for the\par Good Friday holiday.\par     A Reuters poll on Thursday estimated India's inflation rate\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 based on wholesale prices to have fallen to 4.24 percent in the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year to March 27, from 4.30 percent a week earlier. Bonds had   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 earlier run up after a large state-run life insurer bought long   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bonds amid easy money conditions, spurring demand for   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 securities across the curve.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said rupee liquidity remained abundant as the   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  absorbed a huge volume of foreign capital and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade inflows to check the rupee's appreciation on Thursday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                               Thursday's close  Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)      5,838.45\par 5,815.13\par     Indian rupee (/$)             43.6325/6400\par 43.5450/5500\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)          5.1118\par 5.1219\par     Call money (%)                   4.00/4.25\par 4.00/4.25\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)      0.48\par 0.59\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040408e048001o8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
