\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Surges Vs Dlr, But Ends Off Highs; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 15:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose sharply against the dollar Wednesday, breaking several key resistance levels on continued capital inflows and a growing conviction that the government favors a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 However, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended off a 55-month intraday high after a government official called its gains "temporary," and also due to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The rupee broke key psychological barriers against the dollar at INR44.000, INR43.750 and INR43.500, peaking at INR43.355, a level last tested Sept. 2, 1999.  \par \par \uc2 It fell back to end the day at INR43.670, still sharply stronger than Monday's INR44.070. The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was shut Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee's rise was driven mainly by strong and persistent capital inflows following a string of recent privatization sales. The government sold part of its holdings in six state-run companies earlier this month, raising a total of $3.4 billion.  \par \par \uc2 But the local unit gained additional upward momentum Wednesday following comments by a top government official Tuesday, which suggested the government favors a strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as this helps to bring down inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Jaswant Singh said Tuesday that his Bharatiya Janata Party, the leader of India's ruling coalition, "remains committed to a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate" as "a strong rupee has relationships with inflation management and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows."  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has also benefited from notably weak resistance to its rise from state-owned banks, which have bought dollars almost routinely in recent months on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to protect exports.  \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has scaled down its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly because the privatization-related capital inflows aren't speculative investments," a local analyst said. "Also, these inflows aren't debt-creating."  \par \par \uc2 Friday, RBI Governor Y.V. Reddy said the rupee's volatility against the dollar was less than the fluctuations in other international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He also stressed the rise was entirely market-driven - a comment taken by many in the market to mean the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is comfortable with a stronger rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 8.6% against the dollar in the past 12 months on capital inflows and general dollar weakness.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers expect the rupee to continue its uptrend in coming weeks, albeit at a slower pace, with some forecasting it to test INR42.50 in the next year.  \par \par \uc2 "Apart from higher inflows arising due to foreign subscriptions in recent privatizations, we believe a key reason for the recent rise is the (RBI's) limited ammunition to sterilize them," a Citigroup report said  \par \par \uc2 In the forward market, dollar premiums ended slightly lower Wednesday, tracking the dollar's sharp fall in the spot market.  \par \par \uc2 The annualized premium over the spot rate on the one-year forward contract ended at 0.69%, down from 0.72% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Mifor-based interest rate swaps were slightly higher Wednesday, tracking U.S. Treasury yields, with the two-year swap ending 2.64%-2.69% from 2.60%-2.65% at the previous close. Mifor is the Mumbai interbank forward offered rate. It is derived from dollar forward rates.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices gained slightly Wednesday on mild liquidity-led buying. Expectations of stronger demand at the start of the new fiscal year also fueled buying, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year bond yield closed slightly lower at 5.15% compared with the previous close of 5.16%.  \par \par \uc2 Bond prices are expected to gain further in the coming days as banks make fresh investment allocations in the new financial year.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight interbank call money rate ended flat at 4.0%-4.25% amid ample money market liquidity. [ 31-03-04 1356GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Wednesday    Previous \par INR43.67     INR44.07 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums \par May                     September              February \par INR0.1075 vs INR0.1100  INR0.195 vs INR0.200   INR0.285 vs INR0.305 \par  \par Daily Repurchase Auction Amount \par Wednesday         Previous \par INR227.80 Bln     INR456.60 Bln \par  \par Repurchase Auction Cutoff \par Wednesday      Previous \par 4.5%             4.5% \par  \par Call Rate \par Wednesday        Previous Close \par 4.00%-4.25%      4.00%-4.25% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Current Price   Previous Price \par  2-Year Mifor swap   2.64%-2.69%     2.60%-2.65% \par  5-Year OIS          4.77%-4.80%     4.75%-4.80% \par  \par Benchmark Bond Prices \par Security   Maturity   Current Price   Previous Price \par  7.40% GOI   2012        115.16          115.10 \par  7.37% GOI   2014        117.25          117.17 \par  8.07% GOI   2017        124.35          124.30 \par  6.05% GOI   2019        104.73          104.45 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; anil.varma@dowjones.com [ 31-03-04 1357GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument D