\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Rupee Hits Fresh 46-Mo High Vs Dlr; Bonds End Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 16:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee ended at a fresh 46-month high against the dollar Monday on continuing capital inflows, but off the day's peak after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke key resistance at INR44.25 to end at INR44.07 Monday, a level last tested May 23, 2000. It had closed at INR44.47 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 2.6% against the dollar in the past seven trading sessions alone, driven by strong capital inflows following a string of stake sales held recently by the government. It has gained 7.25% against the dollar over the past 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 After the sharp early rise, the rupee retreated slightly on dollar buying by state-run banks on behalf of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or RBI.  \par \par \uc2 "The RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be aimed at avoiding speculation and excessive volatility," said a trader at a local bank. "State-owned banks will probably hold the INR44 level for some time."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers expect the rupee to extend gains in the coming months, albeit at a slower pace than over the past several days.  \par \par \uc2 Some in the market forecast the dollar at INR43.50 by the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 "Right now there is no reason to believe the trend in the rupee will reverse, since economic fundamentals continue to favor it," says Janak Desai, head of treasury at Mumbai-based IDBI Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Desai expects the rupee to gain 2.5% over 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 "We are still positive about the rupee given India's strong economic fundamentals, which should attract more capital inflows," says Irene Cheung, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro Bank in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 In the forward market, dollar premiums ended higher Monday, as companies hedged their future payables at low premiums, following their recent fall.  \par \par \uc2 The annualized premium over the spot rate on the one-year forward contract ended at 0.72%, up from 0.63% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Mifor-based interest rate swaps were slightly higher Monday, tracking forward-dollar premiums, with the two-year swap ending at 2.60%-2.65% from 2.50%-2.55% at the previous close. Mifor is the Mumbai interbank forward offered rate. It is derived from dollar forward rates.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices ended marginally higher Monday on mild liquidity-led buying.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the 8.07% bond due 2017 closed slightly lower at 5.41%, compared with the previous close of 5.42%.  \par \par \uc2 Bond prices are expected to remain in a narrow range before the fiscal year ends Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight interbank call money rate ended flat at 4.0%-4.25% amid comfortable money-market liquidity. [ 29-03-04 1414GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Monday       Previous \par INR44.07     INR44.47 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums \par May                   September             February \par INR0.11 vs INR0.09    INR0.20 vs INR0.16    INR0.305 vs INR0.285 \par  \par Daily Repurchase Auction Amount \par Monday            Previous \par INR456.60 Bln     INR538.80 Bln \par  \par Repurchase Auction Cutoff \par Monday         Previous \par 4.5%             4.5% \par  \par Call Rate \par Monday           Previous Close \par 4.00%-4.25%      4.00%-4.25% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Current Price   Previous Price \par  2-Year Mifor swap   2.60%-2.65%     2.50%-2.55% \par  5-