\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee soars as cbank stays away, shares gain.  \b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Suresh Seshadri\par     BOMBAY, March 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee notched up\par one of its biggest intra-day gains on Friday, soaring to a\par 46-month closing peak on a flood of foreign fund and trade\par inflows even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  refrained from market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The rupee          finished at 44.4700/4800 per dollar, an\par appreciation of 0.6 percent against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par session. Its rise of 1.5 percent in the past five sessions was\par the highest weekly gain in over six years.\par     Analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be waiting for the end\par of heavy foreign investment inflows into a recent spate of\par government asset sales before it resumes its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which says it allows the market\par to determine the exchange rate and only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smoothen\par out volatility, had maintained a firm grip on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  till\par last week, allowing a mere 0.8 percent rise in 11 weeks to\par March 18.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The main reason for their minimal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  must have\par been their knowledge of the huge foreign fund inflows towards\par the IPO bids," a treasury head at a private bank said.\par     "By not buying the dollars at higher levels they prevented\par these funds from gaining an exchange rate advantage as well,"\par he added.\par     Overseas funds had bid heavily at a slew of recent public\par share issues which raised about $3 billion and most remitted\par money for the bids this week.\par  \par     The rupee has now appreciated 2.5 percent against the\par dollar in 2004, building on its 5.2 percent rise last year.\par     Indian shares rose for the second day, as investors began\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 buying into blue-chip stocks ahead of the earnings season, when  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 firms are seen reporting hefty profits. The reporting season  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for the March quarter kicks off next month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The 30-issue Bombay Stock Exchange index rallied  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.1 percent to 5,528.94 points in a broad rally led by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 commodity and auto stocks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Investors are saying, 'Thank God March is over,' because  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they can now look forward to fiscal fourth quarter results and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fresh flows from domestic funds," said Ajit Surana, managing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 director of Dimensional Securities Pvt. Ltd.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run refiner Bharat Petroleum Corp (BPCL.BO) jumped  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.4 percent to 470.25 rupees on expectations that a new  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government will allow the politically sensitive fuel prices to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be hiked after general elections in April-May.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other industrials gained on hopes of robust March sales  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 numbers and strong demand in India's booming economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Associated Cement Companies Ltd (ACC.BO), the largest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cement maker, rose about four percent to 255.35 rupees while  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 leading truck maker, Tata Motors Ltd (TAMO.BO) added nearly  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 three percent to 466.35 rupees. Steel Authority of India Ltd  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (SAIL.BO), the biggest steel producer, rose more than three  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent to 33.15 rupees a share.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although they depend on exports for 70 percent of their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revenues, software firms shrugged off the rupee's gains as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investors cheered the tech-laden Nasdaq index's overnight  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Infosys Technologies Ltd (INFY.BO), the second-largest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 software exporter, rose 2.6 percent to 5,300 rupees and Satyam  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Computer Services Ltd (SATY.BO), the fourth-biggest, gained 4.7  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent to 320.65 rupees.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government bonds ended higher, buoyed by a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 lower-than-expected federal borrowing target for first six  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 months of the next fiscal year starting in April.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The yield on the benchmark 10-year bond             eased\par nearly one basis point to 5.1594 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                              MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                 Friday's close   Thursday's\par close\par      Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)     5,528.94\par 5,414.44\par      Indian rupee (/$)            44.4700/4800\par 44.7400/7450\par      7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)         5.1594\par 5.1675\par      Call money (%)                  4.20/4.40\par 4.25/4.50\par      6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)     0.72\par 0.67\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040326e03q001x7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
