\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY VIEW-Indian rupee to rise to 44.75/dlr by end-March.   \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 04:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, March 24 (Reuters) - Following is a comment on the outlook for treasury markets.   \par \par \uc2 The opinions expressed here are those of the author. They should not be seen as representing the views of Reuters. -   \par \par \uc2 V. RAJAGOPAL, HEAD OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  TRADING, KOTAK MAHINDRA BANK, BOMBAY:   \par \par \uc2 "The rupee should rise to around 44.75 per dollar by the end of the month, though the stance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be crucial.   \par \par \uc2 "In any case, sentiment on the dollar has weakened, with a question mark still hanging over the U.S. economic recovery as employment remains weak and inflation subdued.   \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions, which has accelerated the rupee's rise. If the view sets in that there is not going to be any controlling presence, the rupee could strengthen very rapidly.   \par \par \uc2 (The Indian rupee has gained by 1.6 percent so far this year after rising 5.2 percent in 2003). "Factors supporting the rupee are the expected continuation of the stock market rally - the recent bout of weakness is being regarded as a correction.   \par \par \uc2 "We expect more inflows from foreign investors on that account, and also on account of U.S. interest rates expected to stay at current historical lows.   \par \par \uc2 "Moreover, no concentrated demand for dollars is expected, given the comfort of a strengthening rupee. Hence, dollar supplies will continue to overwhelm the market.   \par \par \uc2 "We have revised upwards our target for the (calendar) year-end to 43.25-43.50 per dollar from 44.0 per dollar earlier, in view of the recent strong rally.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's weakness is expected to continue, and central banks in Asia - including the Bank of Japan - have not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in recent days indicating these expectations.   \par \par \uc2 "If the Chinese yuan is re-valued, it will be a clear signal for further dollar weakness against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." "We feel there is room for the dollar to weaken. The sluggish U.S. labour market remains a disturbing factor, which suggests that growth in corporate profits could be coming from cost-cutting, with jobs being freed up.   \par \par \uc2 "Moreover, the U.S. current account deficit remains chronically high." -.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040324e03o000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
