\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India rupee at 44-month high on foreign shr buying.   \b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     By Anirban Nag\par     BOMBAY, March 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee firmed past\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 45 per dollar on Tuesday for the first time since July 2000 on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 inflows from foreign funds chasing $3 billion worth of recent   \par \par \uc2 public offerings of shares in state-run companies.   \par \par \uc2 Dollar-buying by state banks acting on behalf of the   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was muted, allowing the local unit to gain, they   \par \par \uc2 added.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past two years has   \par \par \uc2 curbed sharp gains by the rupee, but analysts said concerns   \par \par \uc2 about inflationary pressures in the rapidly expanding economy   \par \par \uc2 may have prompted authorities to ease their tight grip on the   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  build record \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 reserves of nearly $110 billion and has kept exports - nearly   \par \par \uc2 11 percent of gross domestic product - competitive.   \par \par \uc2 At 1:10 p.m. (0740 GMT), the partially convertible rupee   \par \par \uc2 was quoted at 44.9275/9375 per dollar, firmer than Monday's   \par \par \uc2 nearly 44-month closing high of 45.0875/0950.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee gained nearly 0.22 percent last week and has   \par \par \uc2 appreciated 1.5 percent against the dollar so far in 2004. It   \par \par \uc2 rose 5.2 percent last year on steady trade remittances and   \par \par \uc2 strong foreign investments in local assets.   \par \par \uc2 "The rupee is rising because of strong inflows into the   \par \par \uc2 local stock market," said Siddharth Mathur, strategist at JP   \par \par \uc2 Morgan Chase, adding that he expected further gains for the   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's overseas weakness, export and foreign   \par \par \uc2 investments and higher external commercial borrowings by local   \par \par \uc2 companies will bolster the rupee in the medium term."   \par \par \uc2 Traders said foreign investors had placed large bids in   \par \par \uc2 recent public offerings, especially from energy companies. That   \par \par \uc2 money is now coming into the country, they said.   \par \par \uc2 India raised over $3 billion by selling stakes in six   \par \par \uc2 state-run companies in February and March, including $2.3   \par \par \uc2 billion from a 10 percent share in the country's top crude   \par \par \uc2 producer, Oil and Natural Gas Corp. It also raised $365 million   \par \par \uc2 from the sale of its stake in gas firm GAIL Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 Data from the capital market regulator showed foreign   \par \par \uc2 funds' purchases of local shares and debt in March totalled   \par \par \uc2 $741 million, taking net investments for the year to over $2   \par \par \uc2 billion. In 2003, they bought a record $7.8 billion in local   \par \par \uc2 assets.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have increased their exposure to India as   \par \par \uc2 Asia's third-largest economy is forecast to grow at more than   \par \par \uc2 eight percent in 2003/04 (April-March) aided by a rebound in   \par \par \uc2 the farm sector after the best monsoon rains in a decade. The   \par \par \uc2 economy expanded by four percent in the previous year.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2 'S CHOICE   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is probably easing its tight   \par \par \uc2 grip over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb inflationary trends.   \par \par \uc2 "It is a choice between hiking interest rates or letting   \par \par \uc2 the rupee appreciate," said Dominique Dwor-Frecaut, director at   \par \par \uc2 Barclays Capital, Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "Given that the economic recovery is still at a nascent   \par \par \uc2 stage, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to let the rupee gain so that the   \par \par \uc2 acceleration in inflationary trends is postponed."   \par \par \uc2 Inflation, as measured by the closely tracked wholesale   \par \par \uc2 price index, has recently eased after hovering around six   \par \par \uc2 percent for most of 2004. Weekly data released on Friday showed   \par \par \uc2 inflation fell to 4.91 percent in the year to March 6, well   \par \par \uc2 below the 6.21 percent peak in January.   \par \par \uc2 But analysts said inflation could rise from May, after   \par \par \uc2 general elections, as domestic fuel prices may be allowed to   \par \par \uc2 rise in line with global prices. State-run refiners have not   \par \par \uc2 hiked politically sensitive fuel prices since January.   \par \par \uc2 The economy is sensitive to global crude prices, currently   \par \par \uc2 at 13-year highs, as it imports 70 percent of its   \par \par \uc2 requirements.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040323e03n0016u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
