\par\par \b \uc2 Indian cenbank eyeing global interest rates - Mohan.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Beverly Mathews   \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 DUBAI, March 20 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan said on Saturday that the country's monetary authorities were closely watching global interest rates, which he said were relevant in determing local rates.   \par \par \uc2 "The statements coming from the U.S. Federal Reserve, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan don't at present indicate (hardening) as there is still good deal of excess capacities," Mohan told reporters on the sidelines of a money market and fixed income conference.   \par \par \uc2 "These central banks have not indicated any hardening of interest rates, but we watch all those things."   \par \par \uc2 Mohan said movements in global rates were relevant to India and these were considered along with local factors while formulating the monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 Although India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lays more emphasis on domestic factors such as inflation to set monetary policy, analysts say a soft global rate environment would support the steady pace of foreign inflows, a bulk of which were being mopped up by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep exports cheap.   \par \par \uc2 The steady \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has led to a glut of rupees in the banking system, supporting bond prices in spite of an economic rebound.   \par \par \uc2 Subdued domestic economic growth in the past three years along with benign interest rates globally had encouraged the Reserve bank of India (RBI) to lower official rates sharply.   \par \par \uc2 The key bank rate-which banks use to price loans-is at a three-decade low of six percent, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight repo rate is at 4.5 percent, lowest since repo auctions were introduced in 2000.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Mohan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to avoid volatility.   \par \par \uc2 "We do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce volatility. We do not have a target nor a range as far as the exchange rate is concerned," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "Volatility in the international market has been very high in the last few months and we continue to have a policy of not having great volatility as we believe that is not good for our markets."   \par \par \uc2 His comments came a day after the Indian rupee rose to a near four-year closing high of 45.1575/1625 per dollar, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from the heavy dollar purchases it had been making in recent months.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040320e03k006he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
