\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Rise On RBI Mohan's Inflation Comment;Call Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 11:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices ended higher Saturday after a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official inflation will continue to fall as earlier expected, in spite of a recent rise fuel prices.  \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of India Deputy Governor Rakesh Mohan reiterated Saturday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast of inflation falling to a 4%-4.5% range by the month-end, brushing aside concerns that high global oil prices could damp the ongoing moderation in the rate.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on the sidelines of a conference of Indian money market participants in Dubai, he said oil prices are unlikely to have any "significant impact" on local inflation in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 Although inflation has come off the eight-month highs tested in January, the bond has been worried in recent weeks that the rate may not fall as much as earlier expected amid rising oil and metal prices.  \par \par \uc2 Annual inflation declined to 4.91% in the week ended March 6, from 5.20% a week earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Mohan's comments fueled late buying in bonds, pulling yields slightly down across the board. The 10-year bond yield ended at 5.14%, down from 5.16% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 With inflation expected to moderate further and liquidity remaining ample, bond prices could gain more in the coming days. However, any sharp rise in prices will probably be partially offset by profit-taking ahead of the March 31 fiscal year-end.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight interbank call money rate ended higher at 4.25%-4.40% Friday, compared with 4.00%-4.25% at the previous close, on banks' demand for funds to meet cash reserve requirements.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate markets were closed Saturday. Friday, the rupee rose to a 43-month high against the dollar on big inflows of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from foreign funds who invested in a string of privatizations recently held by the government.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 45.1800 rupees Friday, a level last tested in August, 2000. It had closed at INR45.2425 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian government sold part of its holdings in six state-run companies earlier this month to raise a total $3.4 billion. A significant part of the sale proceeds are believed to have come from foreign investors.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's big losses against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday also spurred local traders to sell it against the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 An apparent absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has bought dollars through the state-run banks almost routinely in recent months, helped the rupee strengthen.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is expected to rise further in the coming months on capital inflows and general dollar weakness. Dealers say the rupee may gain faster in the coming weeks, unless resisted by the state-owned banks, now that it has broken crucial resistance at the INR45.20 level.  \par \par \uc2 In the forward market, dollar premiums ended higher Friday on continued paying by state-owned banks. The annualized premium over the spot rate on the one-year forward contract ended at 0.54%, up from 0.52% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Mifor-based interest rate swaps ended mostly flat in thin trade Friday, with the two-year swap ending unchanged at 2.48%-2.52%. Mifor is the Mumbai interbank forward offered rate. It is derived from dollar forward rates. [ 20-03-04 1015GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rupee Vs Dollar Close \par Friday       Previous \par INR45.1800   INR45.2425 \par  \par Forward Dollar Premiums \par May                     September              February \par INR0.0625 vs INR0.0525  INR0.120 vs INR0.115   INR0.240 vs INR0.235 \par  \par Daily Repurchase Auction Amount \par Friday            Previous \par INR397.45 Bln     INR423.95 Bln \par  \par Repurchase Auction Cutoff \par Friday         Previous \par 4.5%             4.5% \par  \par Call Rate \par Saturday       Previous Close \par 4.25%-4.40%      4.00%-4.25% \par  \par Interest Rate Swaps  Current Price   Previous Price \par  2-Year Mifor swap   2.48%-2.52%     2.48%-2.52% \par  5-Year OIS          4.75%-4.80%     4.84%-4.88% \par  \par Benchmark Bond Prices \par Security   Maturity   Current Price   Previous Price \par  7.40% GOI   2012        115.15          115.12 \par  7.37% GOI   2014        117.35          117.20 \par  8.07% GOI   2017        124.10          124.00 \par  6.05% GOI   2019        104.00          104.00 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anil Varma, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; anil.varma@dowjones.com [ 20-03-04 1016GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040320e03k0001y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
