\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee bounces back, cash dlr liquidity eases.  \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee bounced from\par early lows on Friday afternoon as dollar demand from importers\par eased and a cash dollar shortage appeared to have ebbed,\par dealers said.\par     Dollar inflows from companies which raised foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par loans in recent days are also lending some strength to the\par local unit, dealers said.\par     At 12:25 p.m. (0655 GMT), the rupee          was quoted at\par 45.2900/3000 per dollar, off 45.3300/3400 in the morning and\par firmer than Thursday's five-week closing low of 45.3125/3200.\par     Dealers said tight liquidity in the cash dollar segment\par caused by persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market and the rollover of forward contracts by exporters had\par led banks to buy the greenback in early deals.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent\par sessions to prevent the rupee from appreciating beyond the\par 45.22 per dollar mark.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Analysts say the dollar-buying spree by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was an effort to keep exports competitive and\par build \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\par     "The demand for dollars, probably from defence equipment\par buyers, seems to have ebbed," said a dealer at a private sector\par bank. "These importers probably paid in the near term forward\par segment, which eased the tight cash dollar liquidity."\par     The one-month forward was quoted at an annualised discount\par of 0.09 percent, narrower than Thursday's close of 0.22\par percent.\par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                           MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                  12:25 p.m.       9:25 a.m.\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)   5,860.73         to open\par     Indian rupee (/$)          45.2900/3000    45.3300/3400\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)       5.2540          5.2458\par     Call money (%)                4.25/4.50       4.40/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)   0.26         to open\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040305e03500126\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
