\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee dips, tight cash dlr liquidity weighs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee fell further\par on Friday morning from a five-week closing low struck the\par previous session, as banks bought the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tide\par over a cash dollar shortage, dealers said.\par     At 9:25 a.m. (0355 GMT), the rupee          was quoted at\par 45.3300/3400 per dollar, down from Thursday's close of\par 45.3125/3200.\par     Dealers said the tight liquidity in the cash dollar segment\par had been caused by persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and the rollover of forward contracts by\par exporters.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent\par sessions to prevent the rupee from appreciating beyond the\par 45.22 per dollar mark. Analysts say the dollar-buying spree by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was an effort to keep exports competitive and\par build \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\par     "The cash dollar shortage haunts again," ING Vysya Bank\par said in its morning commentary .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  "This will make matters\par worse -- the rupee could remain well-offered."\par     The rupee has shed nearly 0.2 percent in the past two\par sessions as the dollar rallied against most major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par hopes that growth is returning to the sluggish U.S. jobs\par market.\par     Analysts said the dollar's recent recovery against the euro\par had resulted in the rupee being slightly overvalued against a\par basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its key trading partners, leaving scope\par for a downward correction in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value.\par  \par     But traders expect foreign funds flowing into the country's\par biggest share sale to prevent a sharp fall.\par     India is selling a 10 percent stake in ONGC (ONGC.BO), the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's most valuable company, at 680 to 750 rupees a share.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It is offering to sell nearly 143 million shares from Friday,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raising at least $2.15 billion.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dollar inflows from companies which raised foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par loans in recent days would also lend strength to the local\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                           MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    9:25 a.m.   Thursday's close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)     to open           5,815.87\par     Indian rupee (/$)           45.3300/3400       45.3125/3200\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)        5.2458             5.2400\par     Call money (%)                 4.40/4.50          4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%) to open               0.22\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040305e035000e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
