\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee down on dlr rebound in global markets.  \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, March 3 (Reuters) - Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drove the Indian rupee to a one-week closing low\par on Wednesday as the dollar rose to the year's highs against\par major global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on hopes of a pick-up in the\par long-dormant U.S. jobs market.\par     The rupee          ended at 45.2800/2900 per dollar, weaker\par than its previous close of 45.2350/2425 and not far from a\par finish of 45.2875/2925 struck on February 23.\par     Dealers said demand for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was mainly from\par state-run banks that normally act on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears concerned with the sharp bounce\par in the dollar, especially against the euro," a dealer at a\par state-run bank said.\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBI) frequently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par check sharp volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. Analysts say the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also meant to protect the competitiveness of\par Indian exports.\par  \par     The United States and the euro zone are India's largest\par trading partners.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected the rupee to recover on Thursday, given\par strong ongoing foreign capital and trade inflows to a\par rapidly-expanding economy.\par     "These levels are very good to sell at and we expect the\par rupee to recover tomorrow," a private bank dealer said.\par     Rupee premiums on forward dollars ended higher, though off\par session peaks, amid increased hedging from importers worried\par over the dollar's recent gains.\par     The annualised premium on the benchmark six-month forward\par closed five basis points higher at 0.48 percent, but was off\par the day's peak of 0.54 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                           MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                Wednesday's close   Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)        5,842.20\par 5,823.17\par     Indian rupee (/$)               45.2800/2900\par 45.2350/2425\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)           5.2462*\par 5.2559\par     Call money (%)                     4.25/4.50\par 4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)        0.48\par 0.43\par     * - yet to close\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040303e033001v3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
