\par\par \b \uc2 Indian fund aims to tackle host of monetary issues.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Beverly Mathews   \par \uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Feb 26 (Reuters) - India is reloading its policy guns with a plan to sell special bonds to absorb excess rupees in the market from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move that may keep Indian markets in check and contain inflation.   \par \par \uc2 Over the next year, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) will sell up to $13 billion worth of market stabilisation bonds issued to soak up excess rupees in the market, rupees that the RBI had sold in the first place. It's a process known as sterilisation.   \par \par \uc2 "The fund is definitely desirable. The RBI needs a tool to suck out liquidity from strong foreign inflows," said Indranil Pan, economist with Kotak Mahindra Bank.   \par \par \uc2 He said the system was awash with cash, raising the risk of higher inflation and an asset price bubble, while putting pressure on bond yields and other market interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 Surging foreign investment and other inflows have boosted the rupee, prompting the RBI to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protect exports as high-potential sectors such as outsourcing take off.   \par \par \uc2 The cash overhang - the cost of limiting the rupee's rise to 5.2 percent in 2003 - threatened a bond market bubble last year, when yields plumbed new lows even as the economy recovered.   \par \par \uc2 "Containing liquidity will limit the risk of asset bubbles while allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Dhananjay Sinha, economist with ICICI Bank.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , among the world's fastest growing economies, has seen \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves surge $32 billion over the past year to a record $107.5 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Reducing the cash surplus will also ease price pressures, now a concern, with annual inflation around six percent.   \par \par \uc2 The market stabilisation bonds are separate from federal borrowings aimed at plugging the budget deficit.   \par \par \uc2 SMOOTHENING THE YIELD CURVE   \par \par \uc2 Better management of surplus cash will give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the leeway to fashion its repo rate into a key monetary signal and smooth kinks at the short end of the yield curve.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI currently uses mostly repos to sterilise inflows. Average daily mop-ups have ballooned to 400 billion rupees this month from around 50 billion rupees a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 But the impact is fleeting and excess cash continues to distort the short end of the yield curve, compromising the effectiveness of the repo rate.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees the repo as a tool for managing temporary cash mismatches and the repo rate has emerged as a signal for short-term market interest rates - a trend the RBI would like to see develop.   \par \par \uc2 Overnight unsecured inter-bank loans often cost less than the repo rate of 4.5 percent at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrows against collateral. Even yields on longer-term instruments such as one-year treasury bills are lower.   \par \par \uc2 "Reduced liquidity will remove these distortions and make the repo rate more credible as a signalling device," said Sinha.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the scheme cannot guarantee the liquidity overhang will recede, as evidenced by China's experience.   \par \par \uc2 "There is definitely a possibility that inflows are much stronger than what we have seen," said Siddharth Mathur, strategist with JP Morgan Securities.   \par \par \uc2 "There is optimism about the Indian economy, and it could get difficult to deal with inflows with only one instrument."    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040226e02q001gk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
