\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee retreats on c.bank, forwards slide.  \b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2004\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Feb 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee weakened on\par Monday from a 3-=   year closing high struck the previous\par session, on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sporadic\par dollar-buying by some private sector corporates, dealers said.\par  \par     The bout of weakness drove other banks to cover short\par dollar positions towards close of trade, they added.\par     The rupee          ended at 45.2825/2875 per dollar, down\par from the previous close 45.2325/2375, a level not seen since\par August 1, 2000.\par     "State-run banks, on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , started to\par buy dollars from the 45.23 per dollar mark and took it to\par 45.26," said a dealer at a government-run bank.\par     "There was a short squeeze towards end of trade which saw\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the rupee weaken further."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept a close vigil over the local unit,  \par \par \uc2 pinning it down around the 45.25 level for much of last week.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the dollar-buying may have been to help fund the  \par \par \uc2 government's early repayment of a $1.3 billion multilateral  \par \par \uc2 loan.  \par \par \uc2 Some said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also aim to maintain the export  \par \par \uc2 competitiveness of Indian goods and services. \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central  \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through a clutch of  \par \par \uc2 state-run banks.  \par \par \uc2 Despite Monday's weakness, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained  \par \par \uc2 0.7 percent against the dollar so far in 2004, mainly on  \par \par \uc2 foreign fund inflows into Indian assets and robust trade  \par \par \uc2 remittances.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have pumped in more than $1.0 billion into  \par \par \uc2 Indian shares and debt this year, on top of the record $7.7  \par \par \uc2 billion they invested in local assets in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the local unit is undervalued by about two  \par \par \uc2 percent on a trade-weighted basis, indicating there may be more  \par \par \uc2 gains in store for the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee could lose further ground on  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday, when demand for cash dollars emerges after banks in  \par \par \uc2 the United States open after the U.S. President's holiday on  \par \par \uc2 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Cash dollar demand from importers was absent on Monday due  \par \par \uc2 to the U.S. holiday. Indian banks route most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign  \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions through counterparts in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Rupee premiums on forward dollars ended lower as exporters  \par \par \uc2 stepped up encashing receivables, given a bearish outlook for  \par \par \uc2 the dollar in the medium term.  \par \par \uc2 The premium on the six-month dollar slid 17 basis points to  \par \par \uc2 end at an annualised 0.20 percent, its lowest close in a month.  \par \par \uc2 It last closed lower than this level on January 13, when it  \par \par \uc2 finished at 0.17 percent.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                 Monday's close     Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)   6,012.35\par 6,011.66\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.2825/2875\par 45.2325/2375\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)      5.3393*              5.2890\par     Call money (%)                  4.00/4.25\par 4.10/4.40\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%) 0.20                  0.37\par     * yet to close\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040216e02g002r6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
