\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee rises early, weekend inflows buoy.  \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2004\par 05:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose in early\par Tuesday trading, as dollar supplies bunched over a long weekend\par offset some initial demand sparked by the dollar's mild rebound\par overseas against the euro, dealers said.\par     At 9:40 a.m. (0410 GMT), the Indian rupee          was at\par 45.3375/3450 per dollar, up from an early trough of 45.3650 and\par higher than Friday's 10-week closing high of 45.3500/3550.\par  \par     Trade resumed on Tuesday after Monday's Republic Day\par holiday.\par     "It (the rupee) should trade in a 45.33 to 45.38 range\par since dollar supplies are good, having accumulated over the\par three-day weekend," a dealer at a state-run bank said.\par     "But they (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) are unlikely to let it rise above\par 45.33."\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intermittently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through\par state-run banks to smooth out volatility and contain the local\par unit's appreciation to help local exporters remain competitive.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders also expect foreign capital inflows to be boosted\par this week as local companies line up overseas equity and debt\par issues after last week's sovereign upgrade.\par     Last week, Ashok Leyland, Associated Cement Companies and\par Bharti Tele-Ventures announced plans to raise around a total of\par $800 billion.\par     India's leading private energy conglomerate Reliance is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also expected to launch a $750 million overseas bond issue this\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week. Traders expect issuances by Indian companies to rise\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after Moody's Investors Service raised the country's long term\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating to investment grade last week. Analysts\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expect this to help lower Indian firms' borrowing costs.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said some dollar demand from local companies\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seeking to meet traditional month-end payments could however\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                             MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                       9:40 a.m.    Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)        to open\par 5,816.64\par     Indian rupee (/$)              45.3375/3450\par 45.3500/3550\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)           5.1337\par 5.1350\par     Call money (%)                    4.40/4.50\par 4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd annualised premium (%)    to open\par 0.56\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040127e01r000xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
