\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Money Market-Factors and flows to watch.   \b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2004\par 08:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) accepted all 43 bids it\par received at Thursday's one-day repo auction for 231.30 billion\par rupees at 4.5 percent. It received no reverse repo bids.\par  - Repo balances outstanding with the RBI after Thursday's\par auction were 302.75 billion rupees, which included 71.45\par billion rupees invested in the 11-day auction held on January\par 12.\par  \par     - Refinance drawn from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the bank rate of\par six percent was nil on Wednesday, unchanged from Tuesday.\par     - There were no balances outstanding under the back-stop\par refinance facility on Wednesday.\par     - There were no open market bond sales by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday.\par     - Banks' cash balances with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  totalled 6.95\par trillion rupees on January 19, the tenth day of the current\par two-weekly reporting cycle.\par     NET INFLOWS/OUTFLOWS\par     Net inflows on Thursday, excluding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  refinance,\par were 15.45 billion rupees.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INFLOWS\par     - 246.55 billion rupees from the reversal of Wednesday's\par one-day repos\par     - 195.37 million rupees as interest on the 10.8 percent\par 2008 federal bonds\par     OUTFLOWS\par     - 231.30 billion rupees towards Thursday's repo\par     ANNOUNCEMENTS\par     - Indian Finance Minister Jaswant Singh said on Wednesday\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflation had peaked after a cyclical rise and he remained   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 confident it would be contained within the target for the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fiscal year to end-March.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Y.V. Reddy, said on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday the inflation projection for the financial year   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ending March 2004 remained unchanged at 4.0-4.5 percent,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 despite a recent uptrend.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Reddy also said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not pegging the\par rupee to the real effective exchange rate (REER).\par     - The Indian government needs to address the issue of its\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fiscal deficit in order to achieve higher growth, said Anne   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Krueger, the International Monetary Fund's first deputy   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 managing director.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - She also said the Indian rupee must be allowed more   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 flexibility and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less in the   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday it had kept   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the cut-off price at its weekly auction of 91-day treasury   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bills steady at 98.95 rupees. The yield at the cut-off price   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was unchanged at 4.2562 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lowered the cut-off price at its   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 two-weekly auction of 364-day treasury bills to 95.80 rupees   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from 95.81 rupees. The yield at the cut-off price rose to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4.3962 percent from 4.3853 percent.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                      12:20 p.m.    Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)       5,712.28\par 5,758.19\par     Indian rupee (/$)              45.4025/4125\par 45.3975/4075\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)           5.1358          5.1404\par     Call money (%)                    4.40/4.50\par 4.40/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium (%)                  0.59            0.77\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par     Indicators:\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves (Jan 9)  : $103.824 bln (+$1.721 bln on\par week)\par     Inflation - wholesale prices (Jan 3) : 6.09 pct yr-on-yr\par     M3 Money supply growth (Dec 26)       : 12.8 pct yr-on-yr\par     RBI advances to government (Jan 9)    :  Nil\par     Rupee's intra-day low       : 49.08/dlr on May 16, 2002\par     Rupee's closing low         : 49.0450/0550 on June 3, 2002\par     Bank rate                              : 6.00 percent\par     Repo rate                              : 4.50 percent\par     Cash reserve ratio                     : 4.50 percent\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par     For a speed guide to Reuters money market coverage, double\par click on , , .\par     For reports on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market,\par          .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040122e01m001mq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
