\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee sets 2-wk closing high, cbank is key.  \b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2004\par 12:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rebounded\par strongly on Wednesday to end at a two-week closing high after\par state-run banks stopped their dollar buying on behalf of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late in the session, dealers said.\par  \par     The rupee          ended at 45.5650/5700 per dollar, well\par up from Tuesday's close of 45.6275/6325.\par     It last closed higher on December 23 at 45.5550/5600.\par     "The moment the state-run banks stepped aside, everyone\par came in and started selling including a lot of traders who had\par been sitting long," a dealer at a private bank said.\par     Traders said strong trade and foreign fund inflows were\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 continuing to exert upward pressure on the rupee and only the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept the unit's  \par \par \uc2 gains in check.  \par \par \uc2 "They have been defending various levels in the recent past  \par \par \uc2 but trying to second guess the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as to how far they  \par \par \uc2 may now allow the rupee to appreciate before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again  \par \par \uc2 would be hazardous," a dealer at a state-run bank said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We expect a broad range of 45.50 to 45.60 tomorrow since\par dollar inflows continue to be very strong," he added.\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 usually conducted to check the rupee's appreciation, an attempt  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to maintain India's export competitiveness, and to curb  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 volatility.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also been buying dollars in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recent weeks for the federal government's overseas debt  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 repayments.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Buoyed by ample \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves that set a record  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of $100.59 billion on December 26, India repaid $2.0 billion in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loans in the October-December period.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the rupee remains undervalued by more than  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 three percent on a trade weighted basis in the backdrop of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar's weakness overseas. This suggests further gains are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 likely for the rupee, they said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Forward dollars continued to become dearer as a cash dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 shortage eased, prompting some banks to transact sell-buy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 swaps.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The six-month dollar finished at an annualised premium of\par 0.02 percent, up from Tuesday's discount of 0.01 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                       MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                            Wednesday's close      Tuesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)    5,957.02\par 5,943.64\par     Indian rupee (/$)           45.5650/5700\par 45.6275/6325\par     7.37 percent 2014 bond (%)       5.1074*\par 5.1192\par     Call money (%)                 4.25/4.50\par 4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount) (%)    0.02\par (0.01)\p