\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee slips on cbank, near fwds up from lows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2003\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased to a near\par three-week closing low on Wednesday as state-run banks mopped\par up robust foreign capital inflows, possibly on behalf of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     The rupee          ended at 45.5850/5900 per dollar, down\par from the previous close of 45.5550/5600. It last closed weaker\par than this level on December 5, when it ended at 45.5975/6075.\par     Indian banks are closed on Thursday for Christmas.\par     "There were good dollar inflows which were absorbed by\par state-run banks," said a chief dealer at a government owned\par bank.\par     Dealers said state-run banks had bought to support the\par dollar from slipping below 45.59 and kept the rupee from\par appreciating despite an easing in month-end demand from\par corporates.\par     Some oil firms and a gas retailing company had increased\par dollar purchases in recent sessions which had helped snap the\par rupee's four-day rally on Monday and kept it under pressure for\par most of Tuesday.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par banks in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb volatility. It has been\par absorbing robust capital inflows into the country in recent\par months which has helped \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves cross the\par $100 billion mark for the first time.\par     Despite the steady \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the rupee has appreciated\par more than 5.2 percent against the dollar in 2003, helped by\par heavy foreign fund inflows of around $7.3 billion, expatriate\par remittances and export earnings.\par     NEAR FORWARDS OFF LOWS\par     Near term forward premiums rose from early lows, after\par state-run banks transacted sell-buy swaps on behalf of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     The one-month forward premium ended at an annualised 0.19\par percent, off an opening low of 0.01 percent, but still lower\par than its previous close of 0.39 percent. Dealers said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been brief causing the forward to ease again\par towards close.\par     Near forwards have risen since the start of the week as\par state-run banks acting on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  conducted\par sell-buy swaps after they traded at discounts in recent\par sessions on fears of a cash dollar shortage at the month-end.\par     "With nationalised (state-run) banks doing sell-buy swaps\par for near months, the month-end cash dollar shortage may not\par materialise to the extent the market has been expecting over\par the past weeks," ICICI Bank said in a commentary made available\par on Wednesday.\par  \par     Traders said the sell-buy swaps in the near term would also\par squeeze short-term domestic money market liquidity.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                               Wednesday's close   Tuesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)       5,641.92\par 5,564.33\par     Indian rupee (/$)              45.5850/5900\par 45.5550/5600\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)          5.1423*\par 5.1423\par     Call money (%)                    4.25/4.50\par 4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium                      0.16\par 0.22\par     * yet to close\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031224dzco0025y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
