\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases early, state banks buy dlr.  \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2003\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee bucked\par expectations to ease in early trading on Wednesday after some\par state-run banks bought dollars, which appeared to be on behalf\par of corporate clients, dealers said.\par     Some oil firms and a gas retailing company had increased\par dollar purchases in recent sessions and traders said the latest\par buying showed their import requirements had not yet been met.\par     "Some state-run banks are buying dollars," said a chief\par dealer at a private sector bank. "We have to see if this is for\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or for state-run companies."\par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par banks in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb volatility.\par     At 9:15 a.m. (0345 GMT) the rupee          was quoted at\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 45.5700/5750 per dollar, down from the previous close of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 45.5550/5600. Traders said volumes were thin as most banks had  \par \par \uc2 scaled down \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the year end.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee had traded weaker for most of Tuesday, dropping  \par \par \uc2 to a session low of 45.6150 before dollar inflows from foreign  \par \par \uc2 funds led to a rebound.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has appreciated more than 5.2 percent against the  \par \par \uc2 dollar in 2003, helped by heavy foreign fund inflows of around  \par \par \uc2 $7.3 billion. The inflows are the highest in any single year  \par \par \uc2 since offshore funds were first allowed to invest in Indian  \par \par \uc2 markets a decade ago.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                  9:15 a.m.  Tuesday's close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts) to open          5,564.33\par     Indian rupee (/$)            45.5700/5750 45.5550/5600\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)    5.1447            5.1423\par     Call money (%)                4.25/4.50      4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium             to open              0.22\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031224dzco000s8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
