\par\par \b \uc2 India c.bank holds rupee, month-end bids eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2003\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 22 (Reuters) - Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the Indian rupee  in check in early\par trading on Monday in a market where volumes had thinned ahead\par of the year-end, traders said.\par     Banks were wary of selling the dollar as they expected\par routine month-end dollar demand from state-run companies to\par meet import requirement, they said.\par  \par     A heightened terror alert in the United States also kept\par trade cautious, they said.\par     "Volumes are low ahead of the year-end and banks are not\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 going short on the dollar as any marginal demand could have an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 exaggerated impact," said a chief dealer in a private sector  \par \par \uc2 bank.  \par \par \uc2 "We could see some commercial dollar demand as the market  \par \par \uc2 gets convinced that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not let the rupee  \par \par \uc2 cross 45.50," he added.  \par \par \uc2 At 9:25 a.m. (0355 GMT), the rupee was quoted at  \par \par \uc2 45.5075/5175 per dollar, barely changed from its previous  \par \par \uc2 finish of 45.5050/5150 which was a five-week closing high.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is up 5.4 percent against the dollar so far in  \par \par \uc2 2003 on foreign fund investments, remittances from Indians  \par \par \uc2 working overseas and exporters' dollar sales. The dollar's  \par \par \uc2 weakness against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also helped the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 Inflows and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee  \par \par \uc2 from appreciating sharply have driven \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 reserves to a record $100.248 billion in the week ending  \par \par \uc2 December 19.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to relax some capital  \par \par \uc2 controls and make the rupee more convertible amid the record  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only convertible on the current  \par \par \uc2 account although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been gradually relaxing  \par \par \uc2 some capital controls in recent years.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                   9:25 a.m.    Previous close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)  to open           5,541.35\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.5075/5175  45.5050/5150\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)     5.1516             5.1572\par     Call money (%)                 4.25/4.50       4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount)   to open              0.05\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031222dzcm000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
