\par\par \b \uc2 India's reserves at new high, close to $100 billion.   \b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2003\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BOMBAY, Dec 20 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to a record high of $98.96 billion on December 12, boosted by foreign investment inflows, trade flows and revaluation gains on the dollar's weakness against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released on Saturday showed reserves climbed $1.44 billion in the week to December 12, notching their seventh straight week of gains and extending rises over the past year to $30.5 billion, or nearly 45 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "The entire rise may not be attributable to money flows, part of it is due to revaluation as the dollar has been depreciating against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Siddharth Mathur, strategist at JP Morgan.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the numbers included the effect of appreciation or depreciation of non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held in the reserves such as the euro, sterling and yen.   \par \par \uc2 The euro has appreciated roughly 19 percent against the dollar this year and hit record highs against the greenback this week. The sterling and the yen are up around 10 percent each against the dollar this year. Analysts expect reserves, currently equivalent to around 20 percent of India's gross domestic product, to touch the psychological $100 billion mark before the end of the year and said the healthy numbers could encourage the country to pay more of its external debt ahead of schedule.   \par \par \uc2 "It makes sense to pre-pay more and to contract our external debt, given the level of reserves," said Mathur.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, an official said the country would pre-pay $1.3 billion to the Asian Development Bank before end-March. A senior government official said earlier this year that India would pre-pay external debt worth nearly $3.0 billion to more than a dozen countries.   \par \par \uc2 Grappling with a problem of plenty, the government earlier this year also tightened its policy on foreign borrowing by Indian companies in what analysts saw as a move to try and stem inflows.   \par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, global rating agency Standard and Poor's raised its outlook on the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to stable from negative, acknowledging the improvement in reserves, although it kept the rating at a speculative 'BB'.   \par \par \uc2 India is places sixth in Asia in terms of reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The rise in reserves, besides the revaluation gains, reflects heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  to mop up inflows from foreign investors, remittances from Indians working overseas and trade flows.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at preventing excessive rises in the rupee, which would affect the competitiveness of Indian exports. But despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupee has risen by around 5.4 percent against the dollar so far in 2003.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have made net investments of some $7.1 billion in Indian assets in 2003, their highest annual investment since local markets were opened to foreign funds a decade ago, on expectations Asia's third-largest economy will expand by over seven percent in the current fiscal year to March.   \par \par \uc2 Deposits by non-resident Indians rose by $2.6 billion in the first half of the fiscal year which started in April but are expected to have grown more slowly since as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut rates on such deposits in September.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031220dzck004v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
