\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases early on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2003\par 05:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was slightly\par weaker against the dollar in early trading on Friday on\par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a market in which\par volumes had shrunk ahead of the year-end, traders said.\par  \par     Traders said an expected test of the 45.50 per dollar level\par did not take place despite strong foreign capital inflows.\par     "It appears the state-run banks do not want the rupee to\par gain to 45.50 even with the rupee undervalued," said a chief\par dealer at a private sector bank.\par     At 9:20 a.m. (0350 GMT), the rupee was quoted at\par 45.5200/5300 per dollar, down from the previous close of\par 45.5100/5175.\par     State-run banks, said by traders to be acting on behalf of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mopped up dollar inflows from foreign funds   \par \par \uc2  and exporters on Thursday and capped the rupee's gains at   \par \par \uc2  45.50.   \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the trend to continue on Friday.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-run   \par \par \uc2  banks to smoothen market volatility. Traders say it has bought   \par \par \uc2  dollars heavily this year to check the rupee's rise as a strong   \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  affects the competitiveness of Indian exports.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee is up 5.4 percent against the dollar so far in   \par \par \uc2  2003, supported by foreign fund investments, remittances from   \par \par \uc2  Indians working overseas and trade flows. The dollar's weakness   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Analysts say the rupee is still under-valued by about two\par percent on a trade-weighted basis.\par     Sentiment on the rupee will remain upbeat in the near term\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as foreign investments, which have been strong this year, are\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to continue on expectations Asia's third-largest\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy is set for sharply higher growth.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign funds have pumped in $7.1 billion so far in 2003\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par into local assets, their highest addition in a single year\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                   9:20 a.m.   Thursday's close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)   to open            5,455.00\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.5200/5300    45.5100/5175\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)     5.1649               5.1649\par     Call money (%)                 4.25/4.50         4.30/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount)   to open                0.12\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031219dzcj000mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
