\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee ends up marginally, cbank curbs gains.  \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2003\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended\par marginally up on Thursday with gains capped by suspected\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but steady foreign fund inflows into\par the stock market and the dollar's fall against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par kept sentiment strong, dealers said.\par     State-run banks, acting on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par capped the rise at the psychologically key 45.50 per dollar\par mark, dealers said.\par     The rupee ended at 45.5100/5175 per dollar, off 45.50\par struck earlier, and marginally firmer than the previous close\par of 45.5100/5200.\par     "It looks like they (the state-run banks) are quite\par determined not to let the rupee cross 45.50 at the moment,"\par said a dealer at a foreign bank.\par     "But there will be upward pressure on the rupee as foreign\par investments continue to be huge and the greenback loses ground\par against other majors."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par banks to smoothen market volatility.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Traders say it has bought\par dollars heavily this year to check the rupee's rise as a strong\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  affects the competitiveness of Indian exports.\par     The rupee is up 5.4 percent against the dollar so far in\par 2003, supported by foreign fund investments, remittances from\par Indians working overseas and trade flows. The dollar's weakness\par against global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also helped the rupee.\par  \par     Analysts say the rupee is undervalued by nearly two percent\par on a trade-weighted basis, implying more gains may lie ahead.\par     Sentiment for the rupee has also been boosted in recent\par sessions after Standard and Poor's revised upward the outlook\par on India's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating earlier this week.\par     Analysts said the improved outlook could draw more foreign\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 capital inflows into Asia's third largest economy, which is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forecast to grow at over seven percent in the current financial  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year to March 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign funds have made net investments of $7.1 billion in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian assets so far this year, more than nine times their net  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investments in 2002. A bulk of the investments has been in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 shares, with the Bombay index up nearly 62 percent in 2003.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Premiums on the forward dollar edged up as a surge in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflows helped improve liquidity, prompting banks to buy the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 greenback to meet an anticipated cash shortage later in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 month, dealers said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The six-month forward ended at an annualised 0.12 percent,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up from the previous close of 0.11 percent, while cash-tom was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dealt at a premium of 3.21 percent, up from par on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                             Thursday's close    Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)   5,455.00            5,418.23\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.5100/5175     45.5100/5200\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)       5.1588 *            5.1870\par     Call money (%)                   4.30/4.50        4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount)     0.12                  0.11\par     * - yet to close\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031218dzci002qd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
