\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee tests 45.50 vs dlr, c.bank eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2003\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended gains\par to test the psychologically important level of 45.50 per dollar\par in early deals on Thursday on rising foreign investments and a\par weak overseas dollar, dealers said.\par  \par     It is, however, unlikely to appreciate much as state-run\par banks are expected to buy dollars, they said.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks to smoothen market volatility. Traders say it has bought  \f28 \par \par \uc2 dollars heavily this year to check the rupee's rise as a strong  \par \par \uc2 local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  affects the competitiveness of Indian exports.  \par \par \uc2 "The rupee tested 45.50 but state-run banks are buying at  \par \par \uc2 this level now and I feel they will protect that level," said a  \par \par \uc2 chief dealer at a private sector bank.  \par \par \uc2 At 9:15 a.m. (0345 GMT), the rupee was quoted at  \par \par \uc2 45.4975/5075 per dollar, off 45.50 struck earlier, and firmer  \par \par \uc2 than the previous close of 45.5100/5200.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee is up 5.43 percent against the dollar so far in  \par \par \uc2 2003, supported by foreign fund investments, remittances from  \par \par \uc2 Indians working overseas and trade flows. The dollar's weakness  \par \par \uc2 against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also helped the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Analysts say the rupee is undervalued by two percent on a\par trade-weighted basis, implying more gains may lie ahead.\par     The rupee had risen for the second straight day on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday with sentiment boosted by an upward revision to the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 outlook on India's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating by Standard and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Poor's (S&P) earlier this week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the improved outlook could draw more foreign  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 capital inflows into Asia's third largest economy, which is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forecast to grow at more than seven percent in the current  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 financial year to March 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign funds have made net investments of $7.1 billion in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian assets so far this year, more than nine times their net  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investments in 2002. They pumped in a net $123.6 million into  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local assets on Tuesday, according to the capital market  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 regulator.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                      MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    9:15 a.m.    Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)    to open            5,418.23\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.4975/5075     45.5100/5200\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)       no quotes           5.1870\par     Call money (%)                   4.40/4.50        4.25/4.50\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount)     to open               0.11\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031218dzci000pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
