\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee seen opening firmer on foreign inflows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2003\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is expected to\par trade with a firm bias on Tuesday on trade and investment\par inflows but gains were likely to be capped by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par traders said.\par  \par     "I think the rupee will trade in a 45.50-to-45.55 per\par dollar range," said a trader at a private bank.\par     "The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 persistently recently and, unless the dollar weakens  \f28 \par \par \uc2 significantly overseas, I do not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will  \par \par \uc2 allow the rupee to rise much," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Sentiment on the rupee was positive as an improved outlook  \par \par \uc2 for Asia's third-largest economy was expected to continue  \par \par \uc2 drawing strong foreign investment inflows while the dollar was  \par \par \uc2 on a weak footing against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "These factors are prompting importers to leave most of  \par \par \uc2 their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposures unhedged and encouraging traders to stay  \par \par \uc2 short on the dollar," the private bank trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Portfolio investments in India have been strong this year.  \par \par \uc2 Net investments reported by these funds in December so far  \par \par \uc2 totalled $598.3 million against $701.4 million through  \par \par \uc2 November.  \par \par \uc2 They have invested some $6.9 billion in Indian assets so  \par \par \uc2 far this year, more than nine times their net investments in  \par \par \uc2 2002. Analysts expect more strong inflows as the economy is  \par \par \uc2 forecast to grow at seven percent in the current fiscal year to  \par \par \uc2 March.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                            MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                    Monday's close  Previous\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)         5,390.88\par 5,315.81\par     Indian rupee (/$)                45.5575/5675\par 45.5450/5550\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)             5.1987        5.1907\par     Call money (%)                      4.25/4.40\par 4.10/4.30\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount)             0.24\par 0.14\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031216dzcg000k6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
