\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee snaps 10-day rally, weakens on c.bank.  \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended weaker\par for the first time in 11 sessions on Thursday following steady\par dollar buying by state-run banks which dealers said was on\par behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     The rupee          ended at 45.5400/5500 per dollar, down\par from Wednesday's 26-day closing high of 45.5200/5300.\par     "The market was very dull and besides the support buying\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from state-run banks, which began at 45.52, there was some  \f28 \par \par \uc2 demand from a state-run power utility," a dealer at a private  \par \par \uc2 bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said most deals were struck in a narrow band  \par \par \uc2 between 45.52 and 45.55 with exporters still preferring to sell  \par \par \uc2 their dollars around the 45.55 level.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee had risen nearly one percent in 10 sessions to  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's close and traders said sentiment in the local  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still good given the healthy foreign fund inflows.  \par \par \uc2 "The only real demand is on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a  \par \par \uc2 private bank dealer said. "With local shares continuing to  \par \par \uc2 rally and foreign funds investing in them, it is just a  \par \par \uc2 question of how much support the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provides to check  \par \par \uc2 the rupee."  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  periodically  \par \par \uc2 through dollar purchases by state-run banks to try and check  \par \par \uc2 the rupee's rise to preserve the competitiveness of local  \par \par \uc2 exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar's slight recovery overseas  \par \par \uc2 following a suspected yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese  \par \par \uc2 authorities also weighed a little on sentiment on the rupee.  \par \par \uc2 The rupee has so far gained 5.34 percent against the dollar  \par \par \uc2 in 2003, on account of robust foreign portfolio and capital  \par \par \uc2 inflows, and trade and expatriate remittances.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have poured in a record $5.7 billion into  \par \par \uc2 Indian shares this year on expectations that growth of more  \par \par \uc2 than seven percent in Asia's third-largest economy will boost  \par \par \uc2 corporate earnings.  \par \par \uc2 Forward dollars ended steady in a lacklustre market as most  \par \par \uc2 bank traders stayed on the sidelines ahead of the holiday  \par \par \uc2 season.  \par \par \uc2 The annualised premium on the six-month dollar ended at  \par \par \uc2 0.04 percent, slightly down from Wednesday's close of 0.06  \par \par \uc2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                              Thursday's close   Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)     5,299.96\par 5,285.54\par     Indian rupee (/$)            45.5400/5500\par 45.5200/5300\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)         5.2100*\par 5.2165\par     Call money (%)                  4.00/4.25\par 4.00/4.25\par     6-mth fwd premium/(discount)         0.04\par 0.06\par     * - yet to close\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031211dzcb0024s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwg