\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee ends at month low, sheds 0.3 pct in wk.  \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2003\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, Nov 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended at its\par lowest close in a month on Friday, after falling 0.3 percent\par over the week on persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders\par said.\par  \par     The rupee          closed at 45.4150/4250 per dollar,\par against Thursday's 45.3850/3950, and last week's 45.2750/2775.\par     "There were enough dollars to meet the demand in the\par market, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued with its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par said a trader at a state-run bank.\par     "Were it not for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the rupee\par would have trended upwards as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows are more than\par outflows, and globally, the dollar is still languishing."\par     The dollar purchases by state-run banks, acting on behalf\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dragged the rupee down from an early high\par of 45.3250 on Friday.\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sustained its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 through the past month to ensure the rupee does not appreciate  \f28 \par \par \uc2 beyond the 45.30 per dollar mark and affect the global  \par \par \uc2 competitiveness of local exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said concerns that the the dollar's weak spell may  \par \par \uc2 reverse if the U.S. economic recovery gains momentum could also  \par \par \uc2 be spurring the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The rupee has appreciated by nearly six percent so far in\par 2003, buoyed by strong trade and investment inflows.\par     Portfolio investment inflows at almost six billion dollars,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 are over eight times the total for 2003. Most of this money has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 chased Indian shares amid expectations of robust economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But after a surge during the earnings season in October,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fresh investments appear to be slowing down, causing some  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 apprehensions among \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In the forward market, the dollar appreciated as earlier\par fears of a dollar shortage proved unfounded.\par     The annualised premium on the six-month dollar ended at\par 0.31 percent, up from Thursday's 0.25 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                          MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                                 Friday's close   Thursday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)      4,865.83\par 4,949.16\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.4150/4250\par 45.3850/3950\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)         5.1075*\par 5.0902\par     Call money (%)                   4.00/4.50\par 2.50/3.00\par     6-mth fwd premium                     0.31\par 0.25\par     * - yet to close\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031114dzbe002ew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
