\par\par \b \uc2 Steel makers lift Indian shares, rupee climbs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2003\par 14:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Suresh Seshadri\par     BOMBAY, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Indian shares rose for the third\par straight session on Thursday, led by steelmakers after leading\par firms reported strong quarterly earnings growth while the rupee\par hit a new three-week high on foreign investment inflows.\par     The benchmark 30-issue Bombay share index          gained\par 0.77 percent to close at 4,780.52 points, taking the marker's\par gains over the past three sessions to nearly two percent.\par     "We had some very good results and the outlook continues to\par be bullish," said Paras Adenwala, head of equity funds at Birla\par Sun Life Asset Management.\par  \par     "We expect this strong performance to continue and that\par should provide momentum to the rally."\par     The Bombay index has climbed about 40 percent in 2003,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 driven by strong foreign fund purchases. Overseas investors are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 betting the farm-reliant economy will show sharply higher  \par \par \uc2 growth this fiscal year after the country got its best monsoon  \par \par \uc2 in a decade.  \par \par \uc2 Net equity purchases by foreign funds total $4.4 billion so  \par \par \uc2 far in 2003, almost six times the $740 million they invested in  \par \par \uc2 the whole of last year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Shares of India's top two steel makers shone after they\par reported huge jumps in quarterly profits.\par     State-run Steel Authority of India Ltd (SAIL.BO), the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 industry leader, spurted 5.6 percent to 44.95 rupees, after it  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reported a net profit of 5.05 billion rupees for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July-September  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 compared with a net loss of 1.58 billion rupees a year  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 earlier.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tata Iron and Steel Company Ltd (TISC.BO), the nation's No  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2 steel maker, climbed 5.2 percent to 347.90 rupees after its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 past quarter earnings doubled to 4.03 billion rupees.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Their traded volumes were the highest on the Bombay\par exchange.\par     RUPEE GAINS, BONDS SLIP\par     The rupee          breached the key psychological 45.30 per\par dollar level buoyed by steady foreign investments in stocks.\par     It finished at 45.2875/2975 per dollar, firmer than\par Wednesday's close of 45.3100/3175. Traders said further gains\par were gains checked by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has bought dollars heavily this\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year to curb the rupee's rise amid fears that the local  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise will affect the competitiveness of domestic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exports. The rupee, which is partly convertible, has risen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around six percent against the dollar so far in 2003.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yields on Indian federal bonds ended slightly higher,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 nudged off early lows on selling sparked by uncertainty over  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the availability of funds.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The benchmark 10-year bond              ended at 5.1018\par percent, compared to Wednesday's 5.0963 percent.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par                             MARKET SNAPSHOT\par                               Thursday's close  Wednesday's\par close\par     Bombay Sensitive Index (pts)      4,780.52\par 4,744.10\par     Indian rupee (/$)             45.2875/2975\par 45.3100/3175\par     7.27 percent 2013 bond (%)          5.1018\par 5.0963\par     Call money (%)                   4.25/4.50\par 6.00/6.25\par     6-mth fwd premium                     0.70\par 0.38\par -------------------------------------------------------------.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031030dzau003b1\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (india near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrd